     About this class:
     Lexer / tokenizer layer of the cBaseFuncLib inheritance chain. Owns:
       - Comment & string-literal detection (DF 2023 comments, multi-line
         comment (slash-star opens, star-slash closes) strings,
         @SQL"""...""" /at-quoted blocks, single/double quote tracking)
       - The tokenizer pipeline (_OverstrikeStrings, _SplitSourceLineToTokens,
         _ConcatenateExpressions, _CollectTokenizerFromProperties)
       - Statement-position extractors (_LeftCommand, _LeftStatement,
         _OfStatement, _ToStatement, _LogicalOperators, _FindCommand)
       - The Tokenizer orchestrator itself (the main public entry point) plus
         HandleMultiLineString and _ChangeLegacyIndicators_Sub.
     Also owns the lexer-state properties used by the tokenizer at compile
     time via function-style accessor: pbIsInPage, pbIsInDF23MultiLineComment,
     pbInCommand, pbInHeader, pbInProcedure, pbInFunction, pbInClass, pbInStruct,
     pbInObject, piMultiLineStringType. Refactoring functions in
     cRefactorFuncLib consume the tokenizer output via the pTokenizer
     property (declared on cBaseFuncLib).
*/
Use Windows.pkg
Use RefactorConstants.h.pkg
Use cRefactorUtilities.pkg

// State enumeration for the _OverstrikeStrings character-scan loop. Guarded
// so re-includes from other packages won't clash with these values.
#IFNDEF eOverstrikeStateOutside
    Define eOverstrikeStateOutside       for 0
    Define eOverstrikeStateInDoubleQuote for 1
    Define eOverstrikeStateInSingleQuote for 2
#ENDIF

/* THE LINE-BY-LINE GUARD, which twenty-eight refactoring functions open with.

   "This line is not code a converter should touch": it is already emitted, it is inside a
   command, it is an image line, or it is a variable declaration. Four terms, and getting one
   of them wrong in one of twenty-eight places is a bug that shows up in one workspace only.

   ByRef, and that matters: tTokenizer carries asLineTokens, so by value this would COPY a
   string array on every line of every file for every function. ByRef passes a reference and
   the struct is never written to here.

   A Define was tried first and cannot work: DataFlex resolves a Define at its own definition
   site, so an expression naming a local fails there with error 4328 - it is not a lazy text
   macro.

   GLOBAL, and that is a measured decision, not a style one. As a class function the call sites
   read LineIsNotCode(Self, &TokenizerData) - an object message send, and this guard is evaluated
   once per selected line-by-line converter per source line: about thirteen million dispatches over
   a 1,379-file workspace. WinServ's first DF26 sweep took 42:29 against 27:35 for the same run on
   2026-08-18, with the per-function line counts identical to within one line and 362 FEWER files
   of grid conversion - so the extra quarter of an hour was not extra work. A global function is a
   direct call with no receiver and no message lookup, and this one reads nothing but its argument,
   so it never needed an object in the first place.

   NOT every guard in the engine is this one. Thirteen others test a SUBSET (bLineIsReady
   alone, or without bIsVariableDeclaration) and four add a FIFTH term (bHasEndSemiColon,
   bIsInStruct). Those are different conditions that merely look alike, and they keep their own
   expressions. */
Function LineIsNotCode Global tTokenizer ByRef TokenizerData Returns Boolean
    Function_Return (TokenizerData.bLineIsReady = True or TokenizerData.bIsInCommand = True or ;
        TokenizerData.bIsInImage = True or TokenizerData.bIsVariableDeclaration = True)
End_Function


Class cRefactorLexer is a cRefactorUtilities
    Procedure Construct_Object
        Forward Send Construct_Object

        // Lexer state. Declared here so cRefactorLexer methods can use the
        // function-style accessor (e.g. pbIsInPage(Self), pbInFunction(Self))
        // at compile time. Get/Set still work from descendant classes via
        // normal inheritance.
        Property Boolean pbIsInPage False
        Property Boolean pbIsInDF23MultiLineComment False
        Property Boolean pbInCommand False
        Property Boolean pbInHeader False
        Property Boolean pbInProcedure False
        Property Boolean pbInFunction False
        Property Boolean pbInClass False
        Property Boolean pbInStruct False
        Property Boolean pbInObject False
        Property Integer piMultiLineStringType MLS_None
        // True when the line the Tokenizer read last is a multi-line string's text or a #HEADER region line
        // (2026-10-29), a line wholly inside a block comment or a report image's text (2026-10-30): the engine
        // hands such a line to no line function, as it does macro code.
        Property Boolean pbKeepLineAsWritten False
        // True when the line the Tokenizer read last opened a multi-line string (2026-10-29): the engine
        // re-tokenizes a line a fix changed, and an @-string's opening line read again opens it again - it holds
        // the string's quote, so it would otherwise read as the string's closing line.
        Property Boolean pbLastLineOpenedString False
    End_Procedure

    // ====================================================================
    // Comment & string-literal detection (cluster 2)
    // ====================================================================

    /* THE LINE SCANNER AND THE FILE WALK (2026-10-29) - how every lane reads the lines of a DataFlex source: where a
       DF 23 multi-line string, an end comment, a DF 23 block comment, a legacy report image, a #HEADER region and
       macro code begin and end.

       ScanSourceLine reads ONE line in one pass, told which multi-line string is open at its start, and answers
       every question about the line at once (tLineScan, RefactorConstants.h.pkg). ScanSourceFile walks a file's
       lines in order, one ScanSourceLine each, and says what each line is (tLineInfo): the one walk behind the
       macro-code guard (MacroCodeFlags, and cRefactorFuncLib's masking), the whole-file functions' kept text
       (KeptTextFlags, MaskKeptText, _CodeOnlyFileLines), the Deep Scan's masking pass and the line pass's
       look-ahead (_SideProductsReadBelow). The Tokenizer reads its lines through ScanSourceLine too, and the line
       checks call it (_CodeOnlyLine, EndComment, _IsDF23CommentStart, _MultiLineStringOpens ...), so every lane
       reads a line the same way. Both keep their state in their locals and parameters, none in properties, so a
       caller that reads only some lines cannot leave them stale.

       MULTI-LINE STRINGS, measured on DataFlex 26 with compile probes (2026-10-24 and 2026-10-29):
       - a """ string's opener ENDS its line and its closer STARTS its line - text after an opener or before a
         closer is error 4346 - and it opens after any statement ('Set psHtml to """', 'Function_Return """',
         'Move ("""', '{ Description = """');
       - an @-string - @"...", @SQL"...", @'...' and @SQL'...' - may run over several lines, and it ends at its
         FIRST closing quote, in the middle of a line too: the rest of that line is code. Nothing escapes that
         quote ("" and \" both end the string), so a line of its text never holds one;
       - a #COMMAND, #DATA or #REPLACE line in a string's text is text: the compiler defines nothing from it.
       A string left open across lines is named by its delimiter: "" none, '"""' a """ string, '"' or "'" an
       @-string. */

    /* One pass over sLine, the multi-line string sOpenIn open at its start ("" for none):
       - inside a """ string the line ends it when it starts with """, and then opens nothing more; inside an
         @-string, at the first closing quote - a line without it is text, whole;
       - inside a block comment (sOpenIn is its opening marker), at the line's first closing marker, wherever it
         stands - a line without one is comment, whole;
       - the rest of the line is code. Its quotes are walked in order, "..." and '...' each running to their own
         closing quote (DataFlex has no escape for either), and a "//" outside every string ends the walk: the
         rest is the end comment. A block comment opened before it runs to its FIRST closing marker, quotes or
         not (measured on DataFlex 26 - an apostrophe in a comment's text used to hide that marker, and every line
         below read as comment, 2026-10-30), and the walk goes on after the marker; with none, the rest of the
         line is the comment (bBlockOpenOut). A comment's text opens no string and holds no end comment, and it
         is no code: sCode blanks it, markers too, and cuts the line where a comment is left open;
       - the line opens a """ string when it ENDS with a """ that stands outside every string before it ('""""'
         and '"TO"""' end in a string's own closing quote and an empty string) and does not start with one (that
         is a closer); it opens an @-string when the string still open at its end began with @" / @' / @SQL" /
         @SQL'. A directive line ('#...') opens none.
       A tab counts as a space. A line with no quote and no slash costs no character loop. bCode asks for sCode
       too. */
    Function ScanSourceLine String sLine String sOpenIn Boolean bCode Returns tLineScan
        tLineScan Scan
        String sCh sNext sQuote sRest sRestSp
        Integer i iLen iStart iFirst iLast iTriple iQuoteAt iAt
        Boolean bAt bTriple bNoOpen

        Move "" to Scan.sOpenOut
        Move "" to Scan.sCode
        If (bCode = True) ;
            Move sLine to Scan.sCode
        Move (Length(sLine)) to iLen
        Move 1 to iStart
        Move False to bNoOpen

        // Inside a block comment: its first closing marker ends it, wherever it stands
        If (sOpenIn = "/*") Begin
            Move (Pos("*/", sLine)) to Scan.iBlockEndAt
            If (Scan.iBlockEndAt = 0) Begin
                Move True to Scan.bBlockOpenOut
                If (bCode = True) ;
                    Move (Repeat(" ", iLen)) to Scan.sCode
                Function_Return Scan
            End
            Move (Scan.iBlockEndAt + 2) to iStart
            If (bCode = True) ;
                Move (Repeat(" ", (iStart - 1)) + Mid(sLine, iLen, iStart)) to Scan.sCode
        End
        // Inside a multi-line string: where does it end?
        Else If (sOpenIn <> "") Begin
            If (sOpenIn = '"""') Begin
                If (Left(Trim(Replaces((Character(9)), sLine, " ")), 3) = '"""') ;
                    Move (Pos('"""', sLine)) to Scan.iCloseAt
                Move True to bNoOpen
            End
            Else ;
                Move (Pos(sOpenIn, sLine)) to Scan.iCloseAt
            If (Scan.iCloseAt = 0) Begin
                Move sOpenIn to Scan.sOpenOut
                If (bCode = True) ;
                    Move (Repeat(" ", iLen)) to Scan.sCode
                Function_Return Scan
            End
            Move (Scan.iCloseAt + Length(sOpenIn)) to iStart
            If (bCode = True) ;
                Move (Repeat(" ", (iStart - 1)) + Mid(sLine, iLen, iStart)) to Scan.sCode
        End

        // The code from iStart on. No quote and no block comment opening: the first "//" and "*/" are the answer,
        // no walk needed.
        Move (Mid(sLine, iLen, iStart)) to sRest
        If (Pos('"', sRest) = 0 and Pos("'", sRest) = 0 and Pos("/*", sRest) = 0) Begin
            If (Pos("/", sRest) = 0) ;
                Function_Return Scan
            Move (Pos("//", sRest)) to iAt
            If (iAt > 0) Begin
                Move (iAt + iStart - 1) to Scan.iCommentAt
                If (bCode = True) ;
                    Move (Left(Scan.sCode, (Scan.iCommentAt - 1))) to Scan.sCode
            End
            Move (Pos("*/", sRest)) to iAt
            If (iAt > 0 and Scan.iBlockEndAt = 0 and (Scan.iCommentAt = 0 or (iAt + iStart - 1) < Scan.iCommentAt)) ;
                Move (iAt + iStart - 1) to Scan.iBlockEndAt
            Function_Return Scan
        End

        // Where a string can open: not on a directive line, and a """ only at the end
        Move (Replaces((Character(9)), sRest, " ")) to sRestSp
        Move (iStart + Length(sRestSp) - Length(LTrim(sRestSp))) to iFirst
        Move (iStart - 1 + Length(RTrim(sRestSp))) to iLast
        If (Mid(sLine, 1, iFirst) = "#") ;
            Move True to bNoOpen
        Move 0 to iTriple
        If (bNoOpen = False and (iLast - 2) > iFirst) Begin
            If (Mid(sLine, 3, (iLast - 2)) = '"""' and Mid(sLine, 3, iFirst) <> '"""') ;
                Move (iLast - 2) to iTriple
        End

        Move "" to sQuote
        Move 0 to iQuoteAt
        Move False to bAt
        Move False to bTriple
        Move iStart to i
        While (i <= iLen)
            Move (Mid(sLine, 1, i)) to sCh
            If (sQuote <> "") Begin
                If (sCh = sQuote) ;
                    Move "" to sQuote
                Else If (bCode = True) ;
                    Move (Overstrike(" ", Scan.sCode, i)) to Scan.sCode
            End
            Else Begin
                If (i = iTriple) Begin
                    Move True to bTriple
                    Move '"""' to Scan.sOpenOut
                    Move i to Scan.iOpenAt
                End
                If (sCh = '"' or sCh = "'") Begin
                    Move sCh to sQuote
                    Move i to iQuoteAt
                    Move False to bAt
                    If (i > 1) Begin
                        If (Mid(sLine, 1, (i - 1)) = "@") ;
                            Move True to bAt
                    End
                    If (i > 4) Begin
                        If (Uppercase(Mid(sLine, 4, (i - 4))) = "@SQL") ;
                            Move True to bAt
                    End
                End
                Else If (sCh = "/" or sCh = "*") Begin
                    Move (Mid(sLine, 1, (i + 1))) to sNext
                    If (sCh = "/" and sNext = "/") Begin
                        Move i to Scan.iCommentAt
                        If (bCode = True) ;
                            Move (Left(Scan.sCode, (i - 1))) to Scan.sCode
                        Move iLen to i      // the rest is the end comment
                    End
                    Else If (sCh = "/" and sNext = "*") Begin
                        // A block comment: to its first closing marker, quotes or not, and the walk goes on after it
                        If (Scan.iBlockStartAt = 0) ;
                            Move i to Scan.iBlockStartAt
                        Move (Pos("*/", Mid(sLine, iLen, (i + 2)))) to iAt
                        If (iAt = 0) Begin
                            Move True to Scan.bBlockOpenOut
                            If (bCode = True) ;
                                Move (Left(Scan.sCode, (i - 1))) to Scan.sCode
                            Move iLen to i      // the rest is the comment
                        End
                        Else Begin
                            Move (i + 1 + iAt) to iAt
                            If (Scan.iBlockEndAt = 0) ;
                                Move iAt to Scan.iBlockEndAt
                            If (bCode = True) ;
                                Move (Overstrike(Repeat(" ", (iAt + 2 - i)), Scan.sCode, i)) to Scan.sCode
                            Move (iAt + 1) to i
                        End
                    End
                    Else If (sCh = "*" and sNext = "/") Begin
                        If (Scan.iBlockEndAt = 0) ;
                            Move i to Scan.iBlockEndAt
                    End
                End
            End
            Increment i
        Loop
        If (bTriple = False and sQuote <> "" and bAt = True and bNoOpen = False) Begin
            Move sQuote to Scan.sOpenOut
            Move iQuoteAt to Scan.iOpenAt
        End
        Function_Return Scan
    End_Function

    // The end comment ScanSourceLine found on sLine, as the Tokenizer keeps it: from its "//" to the end of the
    // line, the trailing blanks off; "" for none.
    Function _ScannedEndComment String sLine tLineScan Scan Returns String
        If (Scan.iCommentAt = 0) ;
            Function_Return ""
        Function_Return (RTrim(Mid(sLine, Length(sLine), Scan.iCommentAt)))
    End_Function

    // Old DF syntax that used "pages", e.g. "/MyPage"
    // A report-image page marker ("/PageName"). Match AFTER leading whitespace: real report
    // images sit INDENTED inside the report object, and the old column-1-only test missed every
    // one of them - so the page never opened and its "/*" terminator was then mis-read as a DF23
    // block-comment START that, with no "*/" after it, sticks ON to end-of-file and makes EVERY
    // converter skip the real code below the image (Nils 2026-07-11: wp_tidsstamptest.rv -
    // Sysdate4 + operators past the image never converted while Deep Scan still flagged them). A
    // '/' followed by a LETTER is unambiguously an image label: no DataFlex statement starts with
    // '/', a '//' comment has '/' as its 2nd char, and a '/*' has '*' - none are letters. Here in
    // the lexer since 2026-10-29, beside the file walk that reads it.
    Function IsImageStart String sLine Returns Boolean
        String sTrim sChar
        Move (LTrim(sLine)) to sTrim
        If (Left(sTrim, 1) <> CS_ImageNameStart) ;
            Function_Return False
        Move (Mid(sTrim, 1, 2)) to sChar
        If (sChar = "") ;
            Function_Return False
        Function_Return (CS_LowercaseAlphabet contains Lowercase(sChar))
    End_Function

    // Old DF syntax that used "pages". To mark end of a page these two characters were used: "/*"
    // Indentation-tolerant to match IsImageStart (Nils 2026-07-11).
    Function IsImageEnd String sLine Returns Boolean
        Function_Return (Left(LTrim(sLine), 2) = CS_ImageNameEnd)
    End_Function

    /* THE FILE WALK. What each line of asCode is (tLineInfo), the lines read in order with one ScanSourceLine each:
       - eKind: a multi-line string's opening line, text or closing line, a #HEADER region line, a block-comment
         line (the line that opens one whole), a report-image line, or code; bBlockOpenIn says a block comment is
         open at the line's start;
       - eMacro: macro code - a #COMMAND..#ENDCOMMAND or a #DATA..#ENDDATA block, both ends included and left open
         to the end of the file as the compiler reads it, or a directive line ('!...'). Case-insensitive.
       A STRING'S TEXT IS NEVER A DIRECTIVE (measured on DataFlex 26): a #COMMAND, #DATA or #ENDCOMMAND line there
       is text - it opens or ends no block - while a directive line there still counts, as the compiler reads the
       exclamation mark even inside a string, and a block the string stands in runs on. Elsewhere a directive is
       macro code wherever it stands - in a block comment, a report image or a #HEADER region too - and macro lines
       move the walk on as any other line does, as they move the Tokenizer on: a string opened in a macro body is
       followed there too. A block comment's or a report image's text opens no string, so a commented-out opener
       cannot hide the code after it, and a block comment ends at its first closing marker, quotes or not. */
    Function ScanSourceFile String[] ByRef asCode Returns tLineInfo[]
        tLineInfo[] aInfo
        tLineInfo Info
        tLineScan Scan
        String sOpen sTrim sLow sBang
        Integer i iLast iBlock
        Boolean bInBlock bInImage bInHeader

        Move (SizeOfArray(asCode) - 1) to iLast
        If (iLast < 0) ;
            Function_Return aInfo
        Move (ResizeArray(aInfo, (iLast + 1))) to aInfo
        Move (Character(33)) to sBang
        Move "" to sOpen
        Move MC_None to iBlock
        Move False to bInBlock
        Move False to bInImage
        Move False to bInHeader
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move LK_Code to Info.eKind
            Move MC_None to Info.eMacro
            Move sOpen to Info.sOpenIn
            Move 0 to Info.iCloseAt
            Move 0 to Info.iOpenAt
            Move bInBlock to Info.bBlockOpenIn
            Move (Trim(Replaces((Character(9)), asCode[i], " "))) to sTrim
            If (sOpen <> "") Begin
                // A multi-line string's text, or its closing line
                Get ScanSourceLine asCode[i] sOpen False to Scan
                If (Scan.iCloseAt > 0) Begin
                    Move LK_StringCloser to Info.eKind
                    Move Scan.iCloseAt to Info.iCloseAt
                    Move Scan.iOpenAt to Info.iOpenAt
                End
                Else ;
                    Move LK_StringText to Info.eKind
                Move Scan.sOpenOut to sOpen
                Move iBlock to Info.eMacro
                If (iBlock = MC_None and Left(sTrim, 1) = sBang) ;
                    Move MC_Directive to Info.eMacro
            End
            Else Begin
                // Macro code
                Move "" to sLow
                If (Left(sTrim, 1) = "#") ;
                    Move (Lowercase(Left(sTrim, 11))) to sLow
                If (iBlock <> MC_None) Begin
                    Move iBlock to Info.eMacro
                    If ((iBlock = MC_CommandBlock and sLow = "#endcommand") or (iBlock = MC_DataBlock and Left(sLow, 8) = "#enddata")) ;
                        Move MC_None to iBlock
                End
                Else If (Left(sLow, 8) = "#command") Begin
                    Move MC_CommandBlock to Info.eMacro
                    Move MC_CommandBlock to iBlock
                End
                Else If (sLow = "#data" or Left(sLow, 6) = "#data ") Begin
                    Move MC_DataBlock to Info.eMacro
                    Move MC_DataBlock to iBlock
                End
                Else If (Left(sTrim, 1) = sBang) Begin
                    Move MC_Directive to Info.eMacro
                End
                // What the line is
                If (bInImage = True) Begin
                    Move LK_Image to Info.eKind
                    If (IsImageEnd(Self, asCode[i])) ;
                        Move False to bInImage
                End
                Else If (bInBlock = True) Begin
                    Move LK_BlockComment to Info.eKind
                    Get ScanSourceLine asCode[i] "/*" False to Scan
                    Move Scan.bBlockOpenOut to bInBlock
                End
                Else If (bInHeader = True) Begin
                    Move LK_Header to Info.eKind
                    If (_IsHeaderEnd(Self, asCode[i])) ;
                        Move False to bInHeader
                End
                Else If (IsImageStart(Self, asCode[i])) Begin
                    Move LK_Image to Info.eKind
                    Move True to bInImage
                End
                Else If (_IsHeaderDeclaration(Self, asCode[i])) Begin
                    Move LK_Header to Info.eKind
                    Move True to bInHeader
                End
                Else Begin
                    Get ScanSourceLine asCode[i] "" False to Scan
                    If (Scan.iBlockStartAt > 0) Begin
                        Move LK_BlockComment to Info.eKind
                        Move Scan.bBlockOpenOut to bInBlock
                    End
                    Else If (Scan.sOpenOut <> "") Begin
                        Move LK_StringOpener to Info.eKind
                        Move Scan.sOpenOut to sOpen
                        Move Scan.iOpenAt to Info.iOpenAt
                    End
                End
            End
            Move sOpen to Info.sOpenOut
            Move Info to aInfo[i]
        Loop
        Function_Return aInfo
    End_Function

    // One Boolean per line of the file walk aInfo: True = macro code (eMacro).
    Function MacroCodeFlagsOf tLineInfo[] ByRef aInfo Returns Boolean[]
        Boolean[] abFlags
        Integer i iLast

        Move (SizeOfArray(aInfo) - 1) to iLast
        If (iLast < 0) ;
            Function_Return abFlags
        Move (ResizeArray(abFlags, (iLast + 1))) to abFlags
        For i from 0 to iLast
            Move (aInfo[i].eMacro <> MC_None) to abFlags[i]
        Loop
        Function_Return abFlags
    End_Function

    /* One Boolean per line of asCode: True = macro code - a #COMMAND..#ENDCOMMAND body including both ends, a
       #DATA..#ENDDATA block including both ends, or a directive line - as the file walk reads it (ScanSourceFile):
       case-insensitive, a block left open runs to the end of the file as the compiler reads it, and a #COMMAND or
       #DATA line in a multi-line string's text opens no block. The macro-code guard's answer (cRefactorFuncLib). */
    Function MacroCodeFlags String[] ByRef asCode Returns Boolean[]
        tLineInfo[] aInfo
        Boolean[] abFlags

        Get ScanSourceFile (&asCode) to aInfo
        Get MacroCodeFlagsOf (&aInfo) to abFlags
        Function_Return abFlags
    End_Function

    // True when the CODE of sLine starts with the exclamation mark - a raw compiler directive. Indentation
    // (spaces and tabs) is skipped; a comment about a directive ('// !A ...') is not one.
    Function IsMacroDirectiveLine String sLine Returns Boolean
        String sCode
        Move (Trim(Replaces(Character(9), sLine, " "))) to sCode
        Function_Return (Left(sCode, 1) = Character(33))
    End_Function

    // DF 23 block-style multi-line comment (slash-star opens, star-slash closes).
    // Just fill the line with hash-marks (#) and return.
    // The tokenizer members bIsMultiLineCommentStart & bIsMultiLineCommentEnd will
    // be Set by the Tokenizer Function, after this function has been called.
    Function _DF23CommentOverwrite String sLine Returns String
        Boolean bIsInDF23MultiLineComment
        String sOverstrikeLine
        Integer iLength

        Move "" to sOverstrikeLine
        Get pbIsInDF23MultiLineComment to bIsInDF23MultiLineComment
        If (bIsInDF23MultiLineComment = False) Begin
            Get _IsDF23CommentStart sLine to bIsInDF23MultiLineComment
            If (bIsInDF23MultiLineComment = False) Begin
                Get _IsDF23CommentEnd sLine to bIsInDF23MultiLineComment
            End
        End
        If (bIsInDF23MultiLineComment = True) Begin
            Move (Length(sLine)) to iLength
            // Just overstrike the content
            Move (Repeat("#", iLength)) to sOverstrikeLine
        End
        Function_Return sOverstrikeLine
    End_Function

    // Is a block comment open at the end of sLine, with one open at its start (bOpenAtStart) or not? The line
    // scanner's reading (ScanSourceLine): a block comment ends at its first "*/", quotes or not.
    Function _BlockCommentOpenAtEnd String sLine Boolean bOpenAtStart Returns Boolean
        tLineScan Scan
        String sOpenIn

        Move "" to sOpenIn
        If (bOpenAtStart = True) ;
            Move "/*" to sOpenIn
        Get ScanSourceLine sLine sOpenIn False to Scan
        Function_Return Scan.bBlockOpenOut
    End_Function

    // New DF 23 comment syntax: does the block comment open at the line's start end on it? At its first "*/",
    // wherever that stands - quotes in a comment protect nothing (measured on DataFlex 26: "the framework's DOM
    // ... */" kept every line below a comment until 2026-10-30) - unless the code after it opens another one.
    // Callers pass the RAW line, before string overstriking.
    Function _IsDF23CommentEnd String sOverstrikeLine Returns Boolean
        Boolean bOpen

        Get _BlockCommentOpenAtEnd sOverstrikeLine True to bOpen
        Function_Return (bOpen = False)
    End_Function

    // New DF 23 comment syntax: a "/*" outside every string literal, before any "//". The Tokenizer calls this
    // on the RAW line, BEFORE _OverstrikeStrings masks string content - without the quotes walked an in-string
    // "/*" (an HTTP "*/*" accept header) OPENED a block comment, and with no real "*/" after it every later line
    // read as a comment and EVERY refactor skipped it (Nils 2026-06-11, `Set psAcceptTypes of h to "*/*"` in
    // wslibrary.pkg). The line scanner's reading (ScanSourceLine), the one every lane reads.
    Function _IsDF23CommentStart String sOverstrikeLine Returns Boolean
        tLineScan Scan

        Get ScanSourceLine sOverstrikeLine "" False to Scan
        Function_Return (Scan.iBlockStartAt > 0)
    End_Function

    Function _IsDoubleQuoteStart String sOverstrikeLine Returns Boolean
        Integer iPosDouble iPosSingle

        Move (Pos('"', sOverstrikeLine)) to iPosDouble
        Move (Pos("'", sOverstrikeLine)) to iPosSingle
        Function_Return (iPosDouble > 0 and (iPosSingle = 0 or iPosDouble < iPosSingle))
    End_Function

    // Returns the number of single or double quotes contained in the "sLine" param.
    { EnumList="{ eSingleQuotes, eDoubleQuotes}" }
    Function _NumberOfStringQuotes String sLine Integer eQuoteMode Returns Integer
        Integer iQuotes
        UChar[] uaLine

        Move (Trim(sLine)) to sLine
        Get _RemoveEndComment sLine to sLine
        Move (StringToUCharArray(sLine)) to uaLine
        If (eQuoteMode = eDoubleQuotes) Begin
            Move (CountArray(Ascii('"'), uaLine)) to iQuotes
        End
        If (eQuoteMode = eSingleQuotes) Begin
            Move (CountArray(Ascii("'"), uaLine)) to iQuotes
        End

        Function_Return iQuotes
    End_Function

    /* DF 23 MULTI-LINE STRING DELIMITERS - the line scanner's (ScanSourceLine, above), which the
       tokenizer (below), the file walk (ScanSourceFile) and with it the whole-file functions, the Deep Scan and the
       macro-code guard all read, measured on DataFlex 26 (2026-10-24 and 2026-10-29): a """ opener ends its line
       and a closer starts its line; an @-string ends at its first closing quote. */
    Function _MultiLineStringOpens String sLine Returns Boolean
        tLineScan Scan

        Get ScanSourceLine sLine "" False to Scan
        Function_Return (Scan.sOpenOut = '"""')
    End_Function

    Function _MultiLineStringCloses String sLine Returns Boolean
        tLineScan Scan

        Get ScanSourceLine sLine '"""' False to Scan
        Function_Return (Scan.iCloseAt > 0)
    End_Function

    // The closing quote of an open @-string of the piMultiLineStringType iType: '"' for @"... and @SQL"...,
    // "'" for @'... and @SQL'...; "" for a """ string or none.
    Function _AtStringQuote Integer iType Returns String
        If (iType = MLS_AtQuote or iType = MLS_SQLDoubleQuote) ;
            Function_Return '"'
        If (iType = MLS_SQLSingleQuote) ;
            Function_Return "'"
        Function_Return ""
    End_Function

    // The piMultiLineStringType of the string sOpen (the line scanner's delimiter, tLineScan.sOpenOut) that the line
    // sOverstrikeLine opens.
    Function _StringTypeOf String sOpen String sOverstrikeLine Returns Integer
        If (sOpen = '"""') Begin
            If (Right(Uppercase(sOverstrikeLine), 7) = '@SQL"""') ;
                Function_Return MLS_SQLTripleQuote
            Function_Return MLS_TripleQuote
        End
        If (sOpen = "'") ;
            Function_Return MLS_SQLSingleQuote
        If (sOpen = '"') ;
            Function_Return MLS_SQLDoubleQuote
        Function_Return MLS_None
    End_Function

    // ====================================================================
    // Tokenizer pipeline (cluster 1)
    // ====================================================================

    Function _CollectTokenizerFromProperties tTokenizer TokenizerData Returns tTokenizer
        Integer iType

        Get pbInCommand                    to TokenizerData.bIsInCommand
        Get pbIsInPage                     to TokenizerData.bIsInImage
        Get pbInFunction                   to TokenizerData.bIsInFunction
        Get pbInProcedure                  to TokenizerData.bIsInProcedure
        Get pbInClass                      to TokenizerData.bIsInClass
        Get pbInStruct                     to TokenizerData.bIsInStruct
        Get pbInObject                     to TokenizerData.bIsInObject
        Get pbIsInSemiColonMultiLineString to TokenizerData.bHasEndSemiColon
        // The same carried flag, kept under its own name: bHasEndSemiColon is overwritten further
        // down with THIS line's ending, so a converter that must know whether this line CONTINUES
        // the previous one (ChangeLegacyIndicators' split Indicate) reads this one instead.
        Get pbIsInSemiColonMultiLineString to TokenizerData.bIsContinuationLine
        Get pbIsInDF23MultiLineComment     to TokenizerData.bIsInDF23MultiLineComment
        Get piMultiLineStringType          to iType
        Move (iType <> MLS_None)           to TokenizerData.bIsInDF23MultiLineString
        Function_Return TokenizerData
    End_Function

    Function _OverWriteStringAdd String sContent String sOverwrite Integer iStart Integer iArrayItem tTokenizer ByRef TokenizerData Returns Integer
        Integer iLength iEnd
        String sChar

        Move (Left(sOverwrite, 1)) to sChar
        If (Right(sOverwrite, 1) <> sChar) Begin
            Append sOverwrite sChar
        End
        Move (Trim(sOverwrite)) to sOverwrite
        Move (Trim(sContent))   to sContent
        Move (Length(sContent)) to iLength
        Move sContent           to TokenizerData.asStringConstant[iArrayItem].sContent
        Move sOverwrite         to TokenizerData.asStringConstant[iArrayItem].sOverwrite
        Move iStart             to TokenizerData.asStringConstant[iArrayItem].iStartPos
        Move (iStart + iLength) to TokenizerData.asStringConstant[iArrayItem].iEndPos
        Move iLength            to TokenizerData.asStringConstant[iArrayItem].iLength
        Function_Return (iArrayItem + 1) // Increase array item for next call.
    End_Function

    // Helper for _OverstrikeStrings: decides the char-scan start state for the
    // current source line when it may be a continuation of an open string.
    //
    // Two independent continuation kinds:
    //   * DF 23 multi-line string (triple-quote / @SQL triple-quote / @"),
    //     tracked by piMultiLineStringType. The whole line is string content;
    //     this helper overstrikes it wholesale and returns True so the caller
    //     returns immediately.
    //   * Old-school ;-continued multi-line string ("..." / '...' opened on a
    //     previous physical line and left unterminated). piSemiColonStringScanState
    //     holds the in-string state to resume; this helper returns False with
    //     iStartState set so the caller's char-scan resumes mid-string and, once
    //     the closing quote is found, continues over any trailing code normally.
    //
    // Returns False with iStartState = eOverstrikeStateOutside when the line is
    // not a continuation (ordinary code, including a ;-continued code line).
    {Visibility = Private}
    Function _OverstrikeMultiLineContinuation tTokenizer ByRef TokenizerData String sText Boolean bHasEndSemiColon ;
        Integer ByRef iStartState Returns Boolean

        Boolean bInDF23MultiLine bIsSqlSingleFlavored
        Integer iType iLength iString iSingleQuotes iDoubleQuotes iSemiColonScanState
        String  sContent sOverwrite sQuote

        Move eOverstrikeStateOutside to iStartState

        Get piMultiLineStringType to iType
        Move (iType <> MLS_None) to bInDF23MultiLine

        // Not a DF 23 multi-line string: this may still be an old-school
        // ;-continued multi-line string. Resume from the in-string scan state
        // the previous physical line ended in. eOverstrikeStateOutside means
        // the previous line left no string open, so a trailing ; there was
        // ordinary code continuation and this line scans normally.
        If (bInDF23MultiLine = False) Begin
            Get piSemiColonStringScanState to iSemiColonScanState
            Move iSemiColonScanState to iStartState
            Function_Return False
        End

        // Was the open multi-line started with an @SQL'...' marker (single-quote flavored)?
        Move (iType = MLS_SQLSingleQuote) to bIsSqlSingleFlavored

        // AN @-STRING'S CLOSING LINE (2026-10-29): its text runs to the FIRST closing quote - nothing escapes it,
        // measured on DataFlex 26 - so the scan starts inside the string whatever else the line holds; counting
        // the quotes (below) read 'World" + "x") to s' as code from its first character. Its text lines do not
        // come here: the Tokenizer returns them first.
        Get _AtStringQuote iType to sQuote
        If (sQuote <> "" and Pos(sQuote, sText) > 0) Begin
            If (sQuote = "'") ;
                Move eOverstrikeStateInSingleQuote to iStartState
            Else ;
                Move eOverstrikeStateInDoubleQuote to iStartState
            Function_Return False
        End

        Get _NumberOfStringQuotes sText eSingleQuotes to iSingleQuotes
        Get _NumberOfStringQuotes sText eDoubleQuotes to iDoubleQuotes

        // -- Wholesale branches: the entire line is string content. --
        // Double-quote-flavored multi-line; no closing quote on this line.
        If (bIsSqlSingleFlavored = False and iDoubleQuotes = 0 and iSingleQuotes < 2) Begin
            Move sText to sContent
            Move (Length(sText)) to iLength
            Move (Repeat(CS_U, iLength)) to sOverwrite
            If (bHasEndSemiColon = True) Begin
                Move (Left(sOverwrite, (Length(sOverwrite) -1))) to sOverwrite
                Append sOverwrite ";"
            End
            Move (SizeOfArray(TokenizerData.asStringConstant)) to iString
            Move sContent   to TokenizerData.asStringConstant[iString].sContent
            Move sOverwrite to TokenizerData.asStringConstant[iString].sOverwrite
            Move 1          to TokenizerData.asStringConstant[iString].iStartPos
            Move iLength    to TokenizerData.asStringConstant[iString].iEndPos
            Move iLength    to TokenizerData.asStringConstant[iString].iLength
            Move sOverwrite to TokenizerData.sOverstrikeLine
            Function_Return True
        End
        // Single-quote-flavored (@SQL'...') multi-line; no closing quote on this line.
        // NOTE: matches the original logic verbatim, which intentionally skipped the
        //       bHasEndSemiColon trim for the single-quote case. Worth revisiting
        //       whether the asymmetry is intentional (single-quoted SQL strings may
        //       never legitimately span a semicolon-continued line in DataFlex).
        If (bIsSqlSingleFlavored = True and iSingleQuotes = 0) Begin
            Move sText to sContent
            Move (Length(sText)) to iLength
            Move (Repeat(CS_E, iLength)) to sOverwrite
            Move (SizeOfArray(TokenizerData.asStringConstant)) to iString
            Move sContent   to TokenizerData.asStringConstant[iString].sContent
            Move sOverwrite to TokenizerData.asStringConstant[iString].sOverwrite
            Move 1          to TokenizerData.asStringConstant[iString].iStartPos
            Move iLength    to TokenizerData.asStringConstant[iString].iEndPos
            Move iLength    to TokenizerData.asStringConstant[iString].iLength
            Move sOverwrite to TokenizerData.sOverstrikeLine
            Function_Return True
        End

        // -- Not wholesale: a closing quote sits on this line. Set the scan's --
        // -- starting state and return False so caller proceeds to char-scan. --
        If (bIsSqlSingleFlavored = False) Begin
            If (iDoubleQuotes = 0) Begin
                Move eOverstrikeStateInDoubleQuote to iStartState
            End
            Else If (Mod(iSingleQuotes, 2) = 0 and iSingleQuotes <> 0) Begin
                Move eOverstrikeStateInDoubleQuote to iStartState
            End
            Else If (Mod(iDoubleQuotes, 2) = 0 and iDoubleQuotes <> 0) Begin
                Move eOverstrikeStateInSingleQuote to iStartState
            End
            Else If (iDoubleQuotes = 1) Begin
                Move eOverstrikeStateInDoubleQuote to iStartState
            End
        End
        Function_Return False
    End_Function

    // Replaces string-literal content in a source line with overstrike characters so
    // downstream refactoring functions can scan the line without quoting surprises:
    //   "abc" -> "___"   (CS_U for double-quoted content)
    //   'abc' -> '+++'   (CS_E for single-quoted content)
    //   Lines that are content of an open DF 23 multi-line string are overstriked
    //   wholesale via _OverstrikeMultiLineContinuation; lines that continue an
    //   old-school ;-continued string resume the char-scan mid-string.
    // Also: removes the end-comment, trims the line, and substitutes Character(9) tabs
    // with a single space (preserving char positions).
    // Returns TokenizerData.sLine unchanged when no quotes are present.
    //
    // Three branches in order:
    //   1. Image-page or DF 23 block-comment line: pass through (no scanning).
    //   2. Open multi-line string continuation (DF 23 wholesale, or old-school
    //      ;-continued resume): delegate to _OverstrikeMultiLineContinuation.
    //   3. Normal line: explicit state-machine scan over each character. State is one of
    //      eOverstrikeStateOutside / eOverstrikeStateInDoubleQuote / eOverstrikeStateInSingleQuote.
    Function _OverstrikeStrings tTokenizer ByRef TokenizerData Returns String
        Boolean bChanged bHasEndSemiColon bHandled
        Integer iChar iLength iStart iString iState iStartState
        String  sChar sText sTrippelDoubleQuote sContent sOverwrite

        // 1. Image-page or DF 23 block-comment: no string scanning, pass through
        //    (or fill with '#' for inside an open block comment).
        If (pbIsInPage(Self) = True or pbIsInDF23MultiLineComment(Self) = True) Begin
            If (pbIsInDF23MultiLineComment(Self) = True) Begin
                Move TokenizerData.sLine to sText
                Move (Length(sText)) to iLength
                Move (Repeat("#", iLength)) to sText
            End
            Else Begin
                Move TokenizerData.sLine to sText
            End
            Set piSemiColonStringScanState to eOverstrikeStateOutside
            Function_Return sText
        End

        // Strip end-comment and normalize the line.
        Get _HasLineEndSemiColon TokenizerData.sLine to bHasEndSemiColon
        Move (Replace(TokenizerData.sEndComment, TokenizerData.sLine, "")) to sText
        Move (Trim(sText)) to sText
        Move (Length(sText)) to iLength

        // 2. Continuation of an already-open multi-line string?
        //    True  => helper filled TokenizerData.sOverstrikeLine; we're done.
        //    False => iState may have been set to eOverstrikeStateInDoubleQuote /
        //             eOverstrikeStateInSingleQuote to tell the scan loop where
        //             to begin (only when continuing into a line that contains the
        //             closing quote).
        Move eOverstrikeStateOutside to iState
        Get _OverstrikeMultiLineContinuation (&TokenizerData) sText bHasEndSemiColon (&iState) to bHandled
        If (bHandled = True) Begin
            Set piSemiColonStringScanState to eOverstrikeStateOutside
            Function_Return TokenizerData.sOverstrikeLine
        End
        Move iState to iStartState

        // 3a. Fast path: a normal (non-continuation) line with no quote characters.
        If (iStartState = eOverstrikeStateOutside) Begin
            If (not(sText contains '"') and not(sText contains "'")) Begin
                Set piSemiColonStringScanState to eOverstrikeStateOutside
                // Tabs -> single space here too (the slow char-scan below does this; the header promises
                // it). Without it a quote-free line kept embedded tabs, so "Move Src<TAB>to Dest" tokenised
                // as one glued "Src<TAB>to" - "to" was never seen as the keyword and an indicator-prefixed
                // Move mangled to "Move (Src<TAB>to)" (destination dropped).
                If (sText contains (Character(9))) ;
                    Move (Replaces((Character(9)), sText, CS_S)) to sText
                Function_Return sText
            End
        End

        // 3b. Character-by-character state-machine scan.
        Move (SizeOfArray(TokenizerData.asStringConstant)) to iString
        Move False to bChanged
        Move 0 to iStart
        For iChar from 1 to iLength
            Move (Mid(sText, 1, iChar)) to sChar
            // Tab characters become a single space IN THE MASK (preserves char positions). sChar keeps
            // the tab: inside a literal it is the literal's own text and goes into sContent as it is.
            // It was swapped for the space as well, so a line rebuilt from its tokens wrote 'Move "a b"'
            // for 'Move "a<TAB>b"' (2026-09-23). Outside a literal sChar is only compared with a quote.
            If (sChar = Character(9)) Begin
                Move (Overstrike(CS_S, sText, iChar)) to sText
                Move True to bChanged
            End

            Case Begin
                Case (iState = eOverstrikeStateInDoubleQuote)
                    If (sChar = '"') Begin
                        // Closing quote: emit captured "abc..." into asStringConstant.
                        Append sContent sChar
                        Get _OverWriteStringAdd sContent ('"' + sOverwrite + '"') iStart iString (&TokenizerData) to iString
                        Move 0 to iStart
                        Move "" to sContent
                        Move "" to sOverwrite
                        Move eOverstrikeStateOutside to iState
                    End
                    Else Begin
                        // Content of "...": overstrike the char in sText with CS_U,
                        // accumulate the original char in sContent.
                        Append sOverwrite CS_U
                        Move (Overstrike(CS_U, sText, iChar)) to sText
                        Append sContent sChar
                        If (iStart = 0) Begin
                            // First content char of a multi-line continuation: the
                            // helper set the starting state but iStart stayed 0.
                            // Append sChar a second time so sContent's length matches
                            // sOverwrite's after the caller wraps it as '"' + sOverwrite + '"'.
                            // (The padding is intentional, not a bug.)
                            Move iChar to iStart
                            Append sContent sChar
                        End
                    End
                    Move True to bChanged
                    Case Break

                Case (iState = eOverstrikeStateInSingleQuote)
                    If (sChar = "'") Begin
                        // Closing quote: emit captured '...' into asStringConstant.
                        Append sContent sChar
                        Get _OverWriteStringAdd sContent ("'" + sOverwrite + "'") iStart iString (&TokenizerData) to iString
                        Move 0 to iStart
                        Move "" to sContent
                        Move "" to sOverwrite
                        Move eOverstrikeStateOutside to iState
                    End
                    Else Begin
                        Append sOverwrite CS_E
                        Move (Overstrike(CS_E, sText, iChar)) to sText
                        Append sContent sChar
                        If (iStart = 0) Begin
                            // Continuation-line first-content padding; see CS_U branch.
                            Move iChar to iStart
                            Append sContent sChar
                        End
                    End
                    Move True to bChanged
                    Case Break

                Case Else
                    // eOverstrikeStateOutside — looking for an opening quote.
                    If (sChar = '"') Begin
                        // Single-line triple-quoted literal """abc""" — skip past
                        // the opening triple. The loop walks the content without
                        // entering a string state, then skips the closing triple
                        // the same way.
                        Move (Mid(sText, 3, iChar)) to sTrippelDoubleQuote
                        If (sTrippelDoubleQuote = '"""') Begin
                            Move (iChar + 2) to iChar
                        End
                        Else Begin
                            // Transition to InDoubleQuote; seed iStart and capture
                            // the opening '"' in sContent.
                            Move eOverstrikeStateInDoubleQuote to iState
                            Move iChar to iStart
                            Append sContent sChar
                            Move True to bChanged
                        End
                    End
                    Else If (sChar = "'") Begin
                        Move eOverstrikeStateInSingleQuote to iState
                        Move iChar to iStart
                        Append sContent sChar
                        Move True to bChanged
                    End
            Case End
        Loop

        // 4. Finalize.
        If (bChanged = True) Begin
            // If the scan started inside a continuation string and ran off the end
            // while still in-string (no closing quote on this line), flush what we
            // captured so it isn't lost.
            If (iStartState <> eOverstrikeStateOutside) Begin
                If (iState = eOverstrikeStateInDoubleQuote) Begin
                    Get _OverWriteStringAdd sContent ('"' + sOverwrite + '"') iStart iString (&TokenizerData) to iString
                End
                Else If (iState = eOverstrikeStateInSingleQuote) Begin
                    Get _OverWriteStringAdd sContent ("'" + sOverwrite + "'") iStart iString (&TokenizerData) to iString
                End
            End

            // Re-attach the trailing semicolon for legacy ;-continued lines.
            If (bHasEndSemiColon = True) Begin
                Move (Left(sText, (Length(sText) -1))) to sText
                Append sText ";"
            End
            Move sText to TokenizerData.sOverstrikeLine
        End
        Else Begin
            Move TokenizerData.sLine to TokenizerData.sOverstrikeLine
        End

        // Persist whether this physical line ended inside an unterminated
        // old-school string literal. Such a string is only valid DataFlex when
        // the line is ;-continued; the next physical line resumes the scan in
        // this state. Anything else (including a balanced string on a
        // ;-continued CODE line) resets to Outside so the next line scans
        // normally.
        If (bHasEndSemiColon = True and iState <> eOverstrikeStateOutside) Begin
            Set piSemiColonStringScanState to iState
        End
        Else Begin
            Set piSemiColonStringScanState to eOverstrikeStateOutside
        End
        Function_Return TokenizerData.sOverstrikeLine
    End_Function

    //  This will overstrike string literals in a sLine with
    //  _ characters for a "string" and + characters for a 'string'
    Function _OverstrikeSimpleLine String sLine Returns String
        Boolean bDoubleQuote bSingleQuote bChanged bComment
        Integer iChar iLength
        String  sChar sText

        Get _IsCommentLine sLine to bComment
        If (bComment = True or Trim(sLine) = "") Begin
            Function_Return sLine
        End

        Move False to bChanged
        Move (sLine contains '"') to bDoubleQuote
        Move (sLine contains "'") to bSingleQuote
        If (bDoubleQuote = False and bSingleQuote = False) Begin
            Function_Return sLine
        End

        Move False to bDoubleQuote
        Move False to bSingleQuote
        Move sLine to sText
        Move (Length(sText)) to iLength
        For iChar from 1 to iLength
            Move (Mid(sText, 1, iChar)) to sChar
            If (sChar = Character(9)) Begin                  // tab characters should be treated as a single space char, this keeps the
                Move (Overstrike(CS_S,sText, iChar)) to sText // position in the string the same.
                Move True to bChanged
                Move CS_S to sChar
            End
            If (bDoubleQuote and sChar= '"') Begin
                Move (Overstrike("_", sText, iChar)) to sText
                Move True to bChanged
                Move "" to sChar
                Move False to bDoubleQuote
            End
            If (bSingleQuote and sChar = "'") Begin
                Move (Overstrike("+", sText, iChar)) to sText
                Move True to bChanged
                Move "" to sChar
                Move False to bSingleQuote
            End
            If (bSingleQuote = False and sChar ='"') Begin
                Move True to bDoubleQuote
            End
            If (bDoubleQuote = False and sChar = "'") Begin
                Move True to bSingleQuote
            End
            If bDoubleQuote Begin
                Move (Overstrike("_", sText, iChar)) to sText
                Move True to bChanged
            End
            Else If bSingleQuote Begin
                Move (Overstrike("+", sText, iChar)) to sText
                Move True to bChanged
            End
        Loop

        If (bChanged = True) Begin
            Move sText to sLine
        End
        Function_Return sLine
    End_Function

    // The index of the expression whose span holds iPos, -1 when none does. Both are positions on the
    // masked line: a string constant's iStartPos, and an expression's once _SplitSourceLineToTokens has
    // re-found it there. Tells a literal that goes back with its expression from one that goes back to
    // a token of its own.
    Function _ExpressionAtPos Integer iPos tExpression[] aExpressions Returns Integer
        Integer iCount iLast

        Move (SizeOfArray(aExpressions) - 1) to iLast
        For iCount from 0 to iLast
            If (iPos >= aExpressions[iCount].iStartPos and iPos < (aExpressions[iCount].iStartPos + aExpressions[iCount].iLength)) Begin
                Function_Return iCount
            End
        Loop
        Function_Return -1
    End_Function

    // Where an expression's placeholder sits GLUED behind something in sToken - the expression followed
    // a name or a literal with no space, 'sndAlias||||', '"logo"|||||||' - or 0. The run of CS_D must be
    // exactly sReplace's length, with another character before it (so never at position 1: a token that
    // STARTS with the placeholder is the caller's other case) and after it or the token's end.
    Function _GluedPlaceholderPos String sToken String sReplace Returns Integer
        Integer i iLen iLast

        Move (Length(sReplace)) to iLen
        Move (Length(sToken) - iLen + 1) to iLast
        For i from 2 to iLast
            If (Mid(sToken, iLen, i) = sReplace and Mid(sToken, 1, (i - 1)) <> CS_D and Mid(sToken, 1, (i + iLen)) <> CS_D) Begin
                Function_Return i
            End
        Loop
        Function_Return 0
    End_Function

    // Splits up the tokens/elements of the input string into two string arrays, but without indentation and end comment.
    // The line will be broken up by spaces " ", *except* for expressions. Each expression will exist as a
    // separate member/item.
    Function _SplitSourceLineToTokens tTokenizer ByRef TokenizerData Returns tTokenizer
        String sOverstrikeLine sReplace sOrg sOverWrite sExpression sToken sSuffix sPrefix
        String[] asLineTokens
        Integer iSize iSizeSC iCount iCountSC iItem iPos iString iStringConstantSize iToken iTokenSize iSameMask iHolder iGlued
        Boolean bFound bFilled
        tExpression[] aExpressions aExpressionsEmpty
        tExpression Expression
        tQuotedString[] asStringConstant
        tQuotedString QuotedString

        // We need to retrieve expressions from the sOverstrikeLine, as they else will
        // be splitted on several items (if expression contains spaces) in the array and
        // we want each expression as one array member.
        Move TokenizerData.sOverstrikeLine to sOverstrikeLine
        Move TokenizerData.sOverstrikeLine to sOrg

        // _ExtractExpression is called recursively. This is why we use a procedure as it simplifies the work for us.
        Send _ExtractExpressions sOverstrikeLine sOrg (&TokenizerData) (&aExpressions)
        // The overstrikeline may have been changed by the _ExtractExpressions function (if concatenated spaces found in expression)
        Move TokenizerData.sOverstrikeLine to sOverstrikeLine
        Move (SizeOfArray(aExpressions)) to iSize
        Decrement iSize

        // Correct expression start positions: recursive calls in _ExtractExpressions compute
        // positions relative to the remaining substring, not the full overstrike line.
        // Re-scan the full overstrike sequentially, masking each found expression so that
        // duplicate overstrike forms (e.g. two identical-looking expressions) resolve correctly.
        If (iSize >= 0) Begin
            Move sOverstrikeLine to sExpression   // working copy of the full overstrike
            For iCount from 0 to iSize
                Move (Pos(aExpressions[iCount].sExpressionOS, sExpression)) to iPos
                If (iPos <> 0) Begin
                    Move iPos to aExpressions[iCount].iStartPos
                    Move (FillString(CS_D, aExpressions[iCount].iLength)) to sReplace
                    Move (Overstrike(sReplace, sExpression, iPos)) to sExpression
                End
            Loop
        End

        // If expressions exists, temporarily replace them with the "|" symbol, before
        // splitting string to array.
        If (iSize <> -1) Begin
            Move aExpressions to TokenizerData.aExpressions
            For iCount from 0 to iSize
                Move (FillString(CS_D, aExpressions[iCount].iLength)) to sReplace
                Move (Pos(aExpressions[iCount].sExpressionOS, sOverstrikeLine)) to iPos
                If (iPos = 0) Begin
                    // OS form not found; fall back to the no-parenthesis variant and correct iStartPos.
                    Move aExpressions[iCount].sExpressionNP to sExpression
                    Move (Pos(sExpression, sOverstrikeLine)) to iPos
                    If (iPos <> 0) Begin
                        Move iPos to aExpressions[iCount].iStartPos
                    End
                End
                If (iPos <> 0) Begin
                    Move (Overstrike(sReplace, sOverstrikeLine, aExpressions[iCount].iStartPos)) to sOverstrikeLine
                End
            Loop
        End
        Else Begin
            Move aExpressionsEmpty to TokenizerData.aExpressions
        End

        // Split string into line tokens array:
        Move (StrSplitToArray(sOverstrikeLine, CS_S)) to asLineTokens
        Move (SizeOfArray(asLineTokens)) to iSize
        Decrement iSize
        // Remove any empty items:
        For iCount from 0 to iSize
            If (asLineTokens[iCount] = "") Begin
                Move (RemoveFromArray(asLineTokens, iCount)) to asLineTokens
                Decrement iSize
                Decrement iCount
            End
            Else If (asLineTokens[iCount] = "]") Begin
                Move (asLineTokens[iCount - 1] + "]") to asLineTokens[iCount - 1]
                Move (RemoveFromArray(asLineTokens, iCount)) to asLineTokens
                Decrement iSize
                Decrement iCount
            End
            Else If (asLineTokens[iCount] = "[" and iCount < iSize) Begin
                // A lone "[" comes from a space right after the bracket, e.g. "[ Found]" splits to
                // "[" + "Found]". Merge it into the NEXT token so the indicator parses identically to
                // "[Found]" (mirrors the lone-"]" merge above, which handles "[Found ]"). Without this the
                // lone "[" seeds an empty FirstBoolean in _ExtractLegacyBooleanContent and the bracket flag
                // is lost, so the line is not refactored at all.
                Move ("[" + asLineTokens[iCount + 1]) to asLineTokens[iCount + 1]
                Move (RemoveFromArray(asLineTokens, iCount)) to asLineTokens
                Decrement iSize
                Decrement iCount
            End
        Loop

        // If there are any string constants, put each one back on its own token. The constants are in line
        // order; a masked token OUTSIDE the expressions takes the next constant that lies outside them too
        // (a position check - the expressions' text is still masked here) and has the token's own mask
        // ("^^" = a two-character "..." literal). Passed over on the way: a constant INSIDE an expression -
        // it goes back with the expression, below - and an empty "" or '', which is never masked, so its
        // token asks for nothing. Until 2026-09-23 exactly ONE inside constant was passed over and the mask
        // was not compared: 'if ((P eq "TP") or (P eq "WA")) move "C" to P' wrote move "WA", and
        // 'Showln "" "Hello"' wrote Showln "" "" (Nils). The mask is replaced IN the token, so a ';' glued to
        // the literal stays, and the token is filled until no mask is left: two literals glued together,
        // "a""b", are one token. Should nothing qualify - positions that do not line up - the first
        // constant with the same mask is taken, and failing that the next in line, whole token, as before.
        Move (SizeOfArray(TokenizerData.asStringConstant)) to iSizeSC
        If (iSizeSC <> 0) Begin
            Decrement iSizeSC
            Move 0 to iCountSC
            Move (SizeOfArray(asLineTokens)) to iSize
            Decrement iSize
            For iCount from 0 to iSize
                Move asLineTokens[iCount] to sToken
                Get _IsOverwriteValue sToken to bFound
                Move False to bFilled
                While (bFound = True and iCountSC <= iSizeSC)
                    Move -1 to iItem
                    Move -1 to iSameMask
                    For iString from iCountSC to iSizeSC
                        If (iItem = -1 and (sToken contains TokenizerData.asStringConstant[iString].sOverwrite)) Begin
                            If (iSameMask = -1) Begin
                                Move iString to iSameMask
                            End
                            Get _ExpressionAtPos TokenizerData.asStringConstant[iString].iStartPos aExpressions to iHolder
                            If (iHolder = -1) Begin
                                Move iString to iItem
                            End
                        End
                    Loop
                    If (iItem = -1) Begin
                        Move iSameMask to iItem
                    End
                    If (iItem <> -1) Begin
                        Move (Replace(TokenizerData.asStringConstant[iItem].sOverwrite, sToken, TokenizerData.asStringConstant[iItem].sContent)) to sToken
                        Move True to bFilled
                        Move (iItem + 1) to iCountSC
                        Get _IsOverwriteValue sToken to bFound
                    End
                    Else Begin
                        If (bFilled = False) Begin
                            Move TokenizerData.asStringConstant[iCountSC].sContent to sToken
                            Increment iCountSC
                        End
                        Move False to bFound
                    End
                Loop
                Move sToken to asLineTokens[iCount]
            Loop
        End

        Move (SizeOfArray(TokenizerData.asStringConstant)) to iStringConstantSize
        Decrement iStringConstantSize
        Move 0 to iString
        Move False to Err
        // If there were any expressions, place them back into the asLineTokens array as items.
        Move (SizeOfArray(aExpressions)) to iSize
        Decrement iSize
        If (iSize >= 0) Begin
            For iCount from 0 to iSize
                Move (FillString(CS_D, aExpressions[iCount].iLength)) to sReplace
                Move (Pos(aExpressions[iCount].sExpressionOS, sOverstrikeLine)) to iPos
                Move (SearchArray(sReplace, asLineTokens)) to iItem
                // Fallback: if exact match failed, scan for a token that starts with the placeholder.
                // This handles cases where trailing chars (e.g. ')' from an outer scope) got attached
                // to the placeholder token after splitting by spaces.
                If (iItem = -1) Begin
                    Move (SizeOfArray(asLineTokens)) to iTokenSize
                    Decrement iTokenSize
                    For iToken from 0 to iTokenSize
                        If (Left(asLineTokens[iToken], Length(sReplace)) = sReplace and ;
                            Length(asLineTokens[iToken]) > Length(sReplace)) Begin
                            Move iToken to iItem
                            Break
                        End
                    Loop
                End
                // Last: the placeholder GLUED behind a name or a literal - 'sndAlias('S', '*')', 'Send
                // AssignFormula of hoReport "logo"('"1"')'. Such a token was never found, and the placeholder
                // was written out; with a literal in front, that literal used to take the whole token back and
                // the argument vanished from the line (2026-09-23, 26 lines in 670,000 of real code).
                Move 0 to iGlued
                If (iItem = -1) Begin
                    Move (SizeOfArray(asLineTokens) - 1) to iTokenSize
                    For iToken from 0 to iTokenSize
                        If (iItem = -1) Begin
                            Get _GluedPlaceholderPos asLineTokens[iToken] sReplace to iGlued
                            If (iGlued > 0) Begin
                                Move iToken to iItem
                            End
                        End
                    Loop
                End
                If (iItem <> -1) Begin
                    // Capture any characters before (glued) and beyond the placeholder (e.g. trailing ')').
                    Move "" to sPrefix
                    If (iGlued > 0) Begin
                        Move (Left(asLineTokens[iItem], (iGlued - 1))) to sPrefix
                        Move (Mid(asLineTokens[iItem], Length(asLineTokens[iItem]), (iGlued + Length(sReplace)))) to sSuffix
                    End
                    Else Begin
                        Move (Replace(sReplace, asLineTokens[iItem], "")) to sSuffix
                    End
                    // Step past the constants that lie BEFORE this expression: the loose ones went back to
                    // their own tokens above, an earlier expression's went back with it. Without this the
                    // first of them was taken for this expression's (Nils 2026-09-23): 'Send Info_Box "AB"
                    // (sA eq "CD")' pasted "AB" into the condition, and with "CDE" the masks no longer
                    // matched, nothing went back, and (sA = "^^^") was written out. An expression that was
                    // not re-found on the line (iStartPos 0) passes nothing over - as before.
                    Move True to bFound
                    While (bFound = True and iString <= iStringConstantSize)
                        Move (TokenizerData.asStringConstant[iString].iStartPos < aExpressions[iCount].iStartPos) to bFound
                        If (bFound = True) Begin
                            Increment iString
                        End
                    Loop
                    If (iString <= iStringConstantSize) Begin
                        Move TokenizerData.asStringConstant[iString].sOverwrite to sOverWrite
                        Move (Pos(sOverWrite, aExpressions[iCount].sExpressionOS)) to iPos
                        If (iPos <> 0) Begin
                            // Rebuild from sExpressionOS (always has masking chars intact, even if
                            // _CreateExpressionVariants pre-substituted a wrong string into sExpression),
                            // then apply the same normalization _CreateExpressionVariants would have:
                            Get TrimInsideSpaces aExpressions[iCount].sExpressionOS to sExpression
                            If (Left(sExpression, 1) <> "(") Begin
                                // Keep trailing semicolon (line continuation char) outside the parentheses.
                                If (Right(sExpression, 1) = ";") Begin
                                    Move ("(" + Left(sExpression, Length(sExpression) - 1) + ");") to sExpression
                                End
                                Else Begin
                                    Move ("(" + sExpression + ")") to sExpression
                                End
                            End
                            // Restore ALL string constants that belong to this expression.
                            // An expression may contain multiple string literals (e.g. typ eq "3" or typ eq "4"),
                            // each overstriked to the same placeholder pattern (e.g. "^").
                            Move True to bFound
                            While (iString <= iStringConstantSize and bFound = True)
                                Move TokenizerData.asStringConstant[iString].sOverwrite to sOverWrite
                                If (Pos(sOverWrite, sExpression) <> 0) Begin
                                    Move (Replace(sOverwrite, sExpression, TokenizerData.asStringConstant[iString].sContent)) ;
                                        to sExpression
                                    Increment iString
                                End
                                Else Begin
                                    Move False to bFound
                                End
                            Loop
                            Move sExpression to aExpressions[iCount].sExpression
                        End
                    End
                    // Restore expression text plus any characters that were before and beyond the placeholder.
                    Move (sPrefix + aExpressions[iCount].sExpression + sSuffix) to asLineTokens[iItem]
                End
            Loop
        End

        Move asLineTokens to TokenizerData.asLineTokens
        // Check if there are any double expressions separated by a "eq|gt|ge|lt|le|ne" logacy operator.
        // If exists, concatenate those expressions into one!
        Get _ConcatenateExpressions (&TokenizerData) aExpressions to aExpressions
        Move aExpressions to TokenizerData.aExpressions

        Function_Return TokenizerData
    End_Function

    Function _ConcatenateExpressions tTokenizer ByRef TokenizerData tExpression[] aExpressions Returns tExpression[]
        Integer iSize iCount iPos iItem1 iItem2 iStart iLength
        String sExpression1 sExpression2 sOperator sOverstrikeLine sOrg sToken1 sToken2 sToken3
        String sExpressionOS sExpressionWS sExpressionNP sExpression sLegacyOperators
        String[] asLineTokens asLegacyOperators
        tExpression Expression1 Expression2
        Boolean bFound

        // There must be at least two expressions in the array for us to check further.
        Move (SizeOfArray(aExpressions)) to iSize
        If (iSize < 2) Begin
            Function_Return aExpressions
        End

        // Check that there is at least one legacay operator in the asLineTokens array.
        Move False to bFound
        Move (SizeOfArray(TokenizerData.asLineTokens)) to iSize
        If (iSize < 3) Begin
            Function_Return aExpressions
        End

        Move "eq|ne|gt|ge|lt|le" to sLegacyOperators
        Move (StrSplitToArray(sLegacyOperators, CS_D)) to asLegacyOperators
        Decrement iSize
        For iCount from 0 to iSize
            Move TokenizerData.asLineTokens[iCount] to sToken1
            Move (SearchArray(Lowercase(sToken1), asLegacyOperators) <> -1) to bFound
            If (bFound = True) Begin
                Move iSize to iCount // We're out of here
            End
        Loop
        If (bFound = False) Begin
            Function_Return aExpressions
        End

        For iCount from 0 to iSize
            // RemoveFromArray below shrinks asLineTokens; the For loop bound is captured statically,
            // so iCount can outrun the new array end. Skip iterations that no longer have room for
            // the `expr1 op expr2` three-token pattern (prevents array out-of-bounds, error 4509).
            If ((iCount + 2) < SizeOfArray(TokenizerData.asLineTokens)) Begin
                Move TokenizerData.asLineTokens[iCount] to Expression1.sExpression
                // Find Expression1 in aExpressions by sExpression field only (SearchArray compares all struct fields):
                Move -1 to iItem1
                Move (SizeOfArray(aExpressions)) to iStart
                Decrement iStart
                For iPos from 0 to iStart
                    If (aExpressions[iPos].sExpression = Expression1.sExpression) Begin
                        Move iPos to iItem1
                        Move iStart to iPos  // break
                    End
                Loop
                If (iItem1 <> -1) Begin
                    Move TokenizerData.asLineTokens[iCount +1] to sToken2
                    Move (SearchArray(Lowercase(sToken2), asLegacyOperators) <> -1) to bFound
                    If (bFound = True) Begin
                        Move TokenizerData.asLineTokens[iCount +2] to Expression2.sExpression
                        // Find Expression2 in aExpressions by sExpression field only:
                        Move -1 to iItem2
                        Move (SizeOfArray(aExpressions)) to iStart
                        Decrement iStart
                        For iPos from 0 to iStart
                            If (aExpressions[iPos].sExpression = Expression2.sExpression) Begin
                                Move iPos to iItem2
                                Move iStart to iPos  // break
                            End
                        Loop
                        If (iItem2 <> -1 and iItem1 < iItem2) Begin
                            // For numeric comparison operators (Gt/Ge/Lt/Le), strip outer parens from left expression:
                            If (Lowercase(sToken2) = "gt" or Lowercase(sToken2) = "ge" or Lowercase(sToken2) = "lt" or Lowercase(sToken2) = "le") Begin
                                Get ReplaceParanthesis Expression1.sExpression to sExpression
                            End
                            Else Begin
                                Move Expression1.sExpression to sExpression
                            End
                            Move ("(" + sExpression * String(sToken2) * String(Expression2.sExpression) + ")") to aExpressions[iItem1].sExpression
                            Move ("(" + aExpressions[iItem1].sExpressionOS * String(sToken2) * aExpressions[iItem1 +1].sExpressionOS + ")") to aExpressions[iItem1].sExpressionOS
                            Move ("(" + aExpressions[iItem1].sExpressionWS * String(sToken2) * aExpressions[iItem1 +1].sExpressionWS + ")") to aExpressions[iItem1].sExpressionWS
                            // Note: This extra parenthesis is later removed by other Tokenizer function logic.
                            Move ("(" + aExpressions[iItem1].sExpressionNP * String(sToken2) * aExpressions[iItem1 +1].sExpressionNP + ")") to aExpressions[iItem1].sExpressionNP
                            Move (RemoveFromArray(aExpressions, iItem2)) to aExpressions
                            Move aExpressions[iItem1].sExpression to sExpression
                            Move (Length(sExpression)) to aExpressions[iItem1].iLength
                            Move sExpression to TokenizerData.asLineTokens[iCount]
                            Move (RemoveFromArray(TokenizerData.asLineTokens, (iCount +1))) to TokenizerData.asLineTokens
                            Move (RemoveFromArray(TokenizerData.asLineTokens, (iCount +1))) to TokenizerData.asLineTokens
                        End
                        // Right-hand side is a literal value (not an expression in aExpressions).
                        // Still concatenate Expression1 + operator + literal and wrap in parentheses.
                        // Example: (dag_arbtid+dag_restid) Ne 0 -> ((dag_arbtid+dag_restid) Ne 0)
                        Else If (iItem2 = -1) Begin
                            If (Lowercase(sToken2) = "gt" or Lowercase(sToken2) = "ge" or Lowercase(sToken2) = "lt" or Lowercase(sToken2) = "le") Begin
                                Get ReplaceParanthesis Expression1.sExpression to sExpression
                            End
                            Else Begin
                                Move Expression1.sExpression to sExpression
                            End
                            Move Expression2.sExpression to sToken3
                            Move ("(" + sExpression * String(sToken2) * sToken3 + ")") to aExpressions[iItem1].sExpression
                            Move ("(" + aExpressions[iItem1].sExpressionOS * String(sToken2) * sToken3 + ")") to aExpressions[iItem1].sExpressionOS
                            Move ("(" + aExpressions[iItem1].sExpressionWS * String(sToken2) * sToken3 + ")") to aExpressions[iItem1].sExpressionWS
                            Move ("(" + aExpressions[iItem1].sExpressionNP * String(sToken2) * sToken3 + ")") to aExpressions[iItem1].sExpressionNP
                            Move aExpressions[iItem1].sExpression to sExpression
                            Move (Length(sExpression)) to aExpressions[iItem1].iLength
                            Move sExpression to TokenizerData.asLineTokens[iCount]
                            Move (RemoveFromArray(TokenizerData.asLineTokens, (iCount +1))) to TokenizerData.asLineTokens
                            Move (RemoveFromArray(TokenizerData.asLineTokens, (iCount +1))) to TokenizerData.asLineTokens
                        End
                    End
                    Move (iCount + 2) to iCount
                    Move (iSize - 2)  to iSize
                End
            End
        Loop

        Function_Return aExpressions
    End_Function

    // ====================================================================
    // Statement-position extractors (consumed by Tokenizer in Batch C)
    // ====================================================================

    // The 1-based position of sWord as a whole word OUTSIDE every parenthesis of sLine; 0 when there is none
    // (_LeftCommand, 2026-10-31). A name holds '#', '$', '@' and '.' as well as what _FindKeywordPos calls a word: the
    // command 'close' stood inside the variable 'close#', and 'if close# close file#' became 'if Begin' (2026-11-02).
    Function _WordPosAtParenDepthZero String sLine String sWord Returns Integer
        String sNameChars sBefore sAfter
        Integer iAt iLeft iRight

        Move (Character(35) + "$@.") to sNameChars
        Move 1 to iAt
        Repeat
            Get _FindKeywordPos sLine sWord True iAt to iAt
            If (iAt > 0) Begin
                Get _NumberOfParanthesis (Left(sLine, (iAt - 1))) (&iLeft) to iRight
                Move "" to sBefore
                If (iAt > 1) ;
                    Move (Mid(sLine, 1, (iAt - 1))) to sBefore
                Move (Mid(sLine, 1, (iAt + Length(sWord)))) to sAfter
                If (sBefore <> "" and Pos(sBefore, sNameChars) > 0) ;
                    Move -1 to iRight
                If (sAfter <> "" and Pos(sAfter, sNameChars) > 0) ;
                    Move -1 to iRight
                If (iLeft = iRight) ;
                    Function_Return iAt
                Move (iAt + Length(sWord)) to iAt
            End
        Until (iAt = 0)
        Function_Return 0
    End_Function

    Function _LeftCommand tTokenizer ByRef TokenizerData Integer eCommandNumber Returns tToken
        Integer iSize iCount iItem iCommand iNumber
        String[] asScopeStart asScopeEnd asCommands
        tToken Data

        If (TokenizerData.bLineIsReady = True) Begin
            Function_Return Data
        End
        Get pasCommands   to asCommands
        // These arrays contains lowercased keywords/scoped words.
        Get pasScopeStart to asScopeStart
        Get pasScopeEnd   to asScopeEnd
        Move -1 to iCommand
        Move 0 to iNumber
        Move (SizeOfArray(TokenizerData.asLineTokens)) to iSize
        Decrement iSize

        For iCount from 0 to iSize
            Move (SearchArray(TokenizerData.asLineTokens[iCount], asCommands, Desktop, RefFunc(DFSTRICMP))) to iItem
            If (iItem = -1) Begin
                Move (SearchArray(TokenizerData.asLineTokens[iCount], asScopeStart, Desktop, RefFunc(DFSTRICMP))) to iItem
                If (iItem = -1) Begin
                    Move (SearchArray(TokenizerData.asLineTokens[iCount], asScopeEnd, Desktop, RefFunc(DFSTRICMP))) to iItem
                End
            End
            If (iItem <> -1) Begin
                If (eCommandNumber = iNumber) Begin
                    Move iCount to iCommand
                    Move iSize to iCount    // Jump out.
                End
                Increment iNumber
            End
            Else If (Lowercase(TokenizerData.asLineTokens[iCount]) = Lowercase(CS_If)) Begin
                Increment iNumber
                // The "If" statement is not included in the pasKeyWords array, but we want it here
                If (eCommandNumber = eFirstCommand) Begin
                    Move iCount to iCommand
                    Move iSize to iCount    // Jump out.
                    Move 1 to iItem
                End
            End
        Loop

        If (iItem <> -1 and iCommand <> -1) Begin
            Move TokenizerData.asLineTokens[iCommand] to Data.sCode
            /* A WHOLE WORD OUTSIDE ANY PARENTHESIS (2026-10-31). A plain Pos found the command 'Open' inside the
               variable 'bOpen', and SplitInlineIfElseLine split 'If (not(bOpen)) Open hTable' into 'If (not( Begin'
               / 'bOpen)) Open hTable' / 'End'. The plain Pos stays for a token that is no word. */
            Get _WordPosAtParenDepthZero TokenizerData.sOverstrikeLine Data.sCode to Data.iStartPos
            If (Data.iStartPos = 0) ;
                Move (Pos(Data.sCode, TokenizerData.sOverstrikeLine)) to Data.iStartPos
        End
        Function_Return Data
    End_Function

    // Get the left part of the line up to but not including the "of or to" part, and not any end comment.
    Function _LeftStatement tTokenizer ByRef TokenizerData Returns tToken
        String sOverStrikeLine
        Integer iPos iItem iEnd
        tToken Data

        If (TokenizerData.bLineIsReady = True) Begin
            Function_Return Data
        End
        Move 0 to iPos
        Move TokenizerData.sOverstrikeLine to sOverStrikeLine

        Move (SearchArray(CS_Of, TokenizerData.asLineTokens, Desktop, RefFunc(DFSTRICMP))) to iItem
        If (iItem <> -1) Begin
            Move (Pos(Lowercase(CS_Of), Lowercase(sOverstrikeLine))) to iPos
            Move (Left(sOverStrikeLine, iPos -1)) to sOverStrikeLine
        End
        If (iItem = -1) Begin
            Move (SearchArray(CS_To, TokenizerData.asLineTokens, Desktop, RefFunc(DFSTRICMP))) to iItem
            If (iItem <> -1) Begin
                Move (Pos(Lowercase(CS_To), Lowercase(sOverstrikeLine))) to iPos
                Move (Left(sOverStrikeLine, iPos -1)) to sOverStrikeLine
            End
        End
        If (iItem = -1) Begin
            Move (SearchArray(CS_As, TokenizerData.asLineTokens, Desktop, RefFunc(DFSTRICMP))) to iItem
            If (iItem <> -1) Begin
                Move (Pos(Lowercase(CS_As), Lowercase(sOverstrikeLine))) to iPos
                Move (Left(sOverStrikeLine, iPos -1)) to sOverStrikeLine
            End
        End
        If (iPos <> 0) Begin
            Move (Left(Trim(TokenizerData.sOverstrikeLine), iPos -1)) to sOverstrikeLine
        End
        If (iPos = 0) Begin
            Move TokenizerData.sOverstrikeLine to sOverstrikeLine
        End
        Move 1                        to Data.iStartPos
        Move (Rtrim(sOverstrikeLine)) to Data.sCode

        Function_Return Data
    End_Function

    // Get the "of xxxx " part from a source line. But not the "to xxx" part and the "of" keyword.
    Function _OfStatement tTokenizer ByRef TokenizerData Returns tToken
        String sOfStatement sOverWrite sLine
        Integer iPos iCount iStart iItem iEnd
        tToken Data

        If (TokenizerData.bLineIsReady = True) Begin
            Function_Return Data
        End
        Move (SearchArray(CS_Of, TokenizerData.asLineTokens, Desktop, RefFunc(DFSTRICMP))) to iItem
        If (iItem = -1) Begin
            Function_Return Data
        End
        Move (iItem + 1) to iStart
        Move (SizeOfArray(TokenizerData.asLineTokens)) to iEnd
        Decrement iEnd
        Move (SearchArray(CS_To, TokenizerData.asLineTokens, Desktop, RefFunc(DFSTRICMP))) to iItem
        If (iItem <> -1) Begin
            Move (iItem -1) to iEnd
        End

        For iCount from iStart to iEnd
            Append sOfStatement TokenizerData.asLineTokens[iCount] " "
        Loop
        Move (Rtrim(sOfStatement)) to Data.sCode
        Move (Pos(Lowercase(CS_Of * String(Data.sCode)), Trim(Lowercase(TokenizerData.sLine)))) to iStart
        Move (iStart + 2)          to Data.iStartPos // "Of" = +2

        Function_Return Data
    End_Function

    // Get the "to xxx" part, but without the "to" keyword.
    Function _ToStatement tTokenizer ByRef TokenizerData Returns tToken
        String sToStatement sOverWrite sLine
        Integer iPos iSize iCount iStart iItem iEnd
        tToken Data

        If (TokenizerData.bLineIsReady = True) Begin
            Function_Return Data
        End
        Move (SearchArray(CS_To, TokenizerData.asLineTokens, Desktop, RefFunc(DFSTRICMP))) to iItem
        If (iItem = -1) Begin
            Function_Return Data
        End

        Move (iItem + 1) to iStart
        Move (SizeOfArray(TokenizerData.asLineTokens)) to iSize
        Decrement iSize
        For iCount from iStart to iSize
            Append sToStatement TokenizerData.asLineTokens[iCount] " "
        Loop

        Move (Pos(Lowercase(CS_To * String(Data.sCode)), Trim(Lowercase(TokenizerData.sLine)))) to iStart
        Move (iStart + 2)         to Data.iStartPos // "Of" = +2
        Move (Trim(sToStatement)) to Data.sCode

        Function_Return Data
    End_Function

    // Pass only the code part of a source line.
    // Returns True if the code contains any of "gt, ge, lt, le, eq, ne" OR ">, >=, <, <=, =, <>"
    // It returns a tOperatorsInfo struct with; bisOperator, bIsLegacy, iPos and sOperator.
    // Note: It only looks for the first occurance of a logical operator in the passed sLine parameter.
    Function _LogicalOperators tTokenizer ByRef TokenizerData Returns tOperatorsInfo
        Boolean bHas
        tOperatorsInfo OperatorsInfo
        String sOverStrikeLine

        If (TokenizerData.bIsBlank = True or TokenizerData.bIsComment = True) Begin
            Function_Return OperatorsInfo
        End
        Move TokenizerData.sOverstrikeLine to sOverStrikeLine
        Get _RemoveEndComment sOverStrikeLine to sOverStrikeLine
        Move (Lowercase(sOverStrikeLine)) to sOverStrikeLine

        Case Begin
            // "Legacy" operators;
            Case (sOverstrikeLine contains " gt ")
                Move (Pos(" gt ", sOverstrikeLine))   to OperatorsInfo.iPos
                Move True                   to OperatorsInfo.bIsOperator
                Move True                   to OperatorsInfo.bIsLegacy
                Move "gt"                   to OperatorsInfo.sOperator
                Case Break
            Case (sOverstrikeLine contains " ge ")
                Move (Pos(" ge ", sOverstrikeLine))   to OperatorsInfo.iPos
                Move True                   to OperatorsInfo.bIsOperator
                Move True                   to OperatorsInfo.bIsLegacy
                Move "ge"                   to OperatorsInfo.sOperator
                Case Break
            Case (sOverstrikeLine contains " lt ")
                Move (Pos(" lt ", sOverstrikeLine))   to OperatorsInfo.iPos
                Move True                   to OperatorsInfo.bIsOperator
                Move True                   to OperatorsInfo.bIsLegacy
                Move "lt"                   to OperatorsInfo.sOperator
                Case Break
            Case (sOverstrikeLine contains " le ")
                Move (Pos(" le ", sOverstrikeLine))   to OperatorsInfo.iPos
                Move True                   to OperatorsInfo.bIsOperator
                Move True                   to OperatorsInfo.bIsLegacy
                Move "le"                   to OperatorsInfo.sOperator
                Case Break
            Case (sOverstrikeLine contains " eq ")
                Move (Pos(" eq ", sOverstrikeLine))   to OperatorsInfo.iPos
                Move True                   to OperatorsInfo.bIsOperator
                Move True                   to OperatorsInfo.bIsLegacy
                Move "eq"                   to OperatorsInfo.sOperator
                Case Break
            Case (sOverstrikeLine contains " ne ")
                Move (Pos(" ne ", sOverstrikeLine))   to OperatorsInfo.iPos
                Move True                   to OperatorsInfo.bIsOperator
                Move True                   to OperatorsInfo.bIsLegacy
                Move "ne"                   to OperatorsInfo.sOperator
                Case Break

            // "Modern" operators;
            Case (sOverstrikeLine contains ">")
                Move (Pos(">", sOverstrikeLine))      to OperatorsInfo.iPos
                Move True                   to OperatorsInfo.bIsOperator
                Move False                  to OperatorsInfo.bIsLegacy
                Move ">"                    to OperatorsInfo.sOperator
                Case Break
            Case (sOverstrikeLine contains ">=")
                Move (Pos(">=", sOverstrikeLine))     to OperatorsInfo.iPos
                Move True                   to OperatorsInfo.bIsOperator
                Move False                  to OperatorsInfo.bIsLegacy
                Move ">="                   to OperatorsInfo.sOperator
                Case Break
            Case (sOverstrikeLine contains "<")
                Move (Pos("<", sOverstrikeLine))      to OperatorsInfo.iPos
                Move True                   to OperatorsInfo.bIsOperator
                Move False                  to OperatorsInfo.bIsLegacy
                Move "<"                    to OperatorsInfo.sOperator
                Case Break
            Case (sOverstrikeLine contains "<=")
                Move (Pos("<=", sOverstrikeLine))     to OperatorsInfo.iPos
                Move True                   to OperatorsInfo.bIsOperator
                Move False                  to OperatorsInfo.bIsLegacy
                Move "<="                   to OperatorsInfo.sOperator
                Case Break
            Case (sOverstrikeLine contains "=")
                Move (Pos("=", sOverstrikeLine))      to OperatorsInfo.iPos
                Move True                   to OperatorsInfo.bIsOperator
                Move False                  to OperatorsInfo.bIsLegacy
                Move "="                    to OperatorsInfo.sOperator
                Case Break
            Case (sOverstrikeLine contains "<>")
                Move (Pos("<>", sOverstrikeLine))     to OperatorsInfo.iPos
                Move True                   to OperatorsInfo.bIsOperator
                Move False                  to OperatorsInfo.bIsLegacy
                Move "<>"                   to OperatorsInfo.sOperator
                Case Break
            Case Else
                Move -1                     to OperatorsInfo.iPos
                Move False                  to OperatorsInfo.bIsOperator
                Move False                  to OperatorsInfo.bIsLegacy
                Move ""                     to OperatorsInfo.sOperator
        Case End

        Function_Return OperatorsInfo
    End_Function

    // Searches for the first DataFlex command in a source line.
    // Returns the Pos or 0 if not found.
    Function _FindCommand tTokenizer ByRef TokenizerData String sSource Returns Integer
        Integer iSize iPos iTest iLength
        String  sToken sLowerCase
        String[] asCommands

        Move 0 to iPos
        Get pasCommands to asCommands
        Move (Length(sSource)) to iLength
        Move (SizeOfArray(TokenizerData.asLineTokens)) to iSize
        Decrement iSize

        While (iLength > 0)
            Move (Pos(" ", sSource)) to iPos
            If (iPos > 0) Begin
                Move (Left(sSource, (iPos -1))) to sToken
                Move (Pos(Lowercase(sToken), Lowercase(sSource))) to iPos
                Move (Trim(Lowercase(sToken))) to sLowerCase
                Move (SearchArray(sLowerCase, asCommands)) to iTest
                // If command not found, try next "word" in sSource;
                If (iTest = -1) Begin
                    Move (Pos(" ", sSource)) to iPos
                    Move (Mid(sSource, iLength, iPos)) to sSource
                    Move (Trim(sSource)) to sSource
                    Move (Length(sSource)) to iLength
                End
                Else Begin
                    Move 0 to iLength // Jump out.
                End
            End
            Else Begin
                Move 0 to iLength // Jump out.
            End
        Loop

        Function_Return iPos
    End_Function

    // ====================================================================
    // Legacy indicator rewriter (helper for ChangeLegacyIndicators)
    // ====================================================================

    // Negate a loop-back condition to the post-test 'Until (...)' EXIT condition for a '[cond] Loop' conversion.
    // A legacy '[cond] Loop' jumps back to Repeat WHILE cond, so the modern equivalent is 'Repeat ... Until
    // (Not(cond))' - NOT a bare 'Loop' (which drops the exit test and spins forever; LegacyApp files.nui
    // '[~seqeof] loop'). The input is the ALREADY parenthesised loop-back condition (the bracket pass resolved
    // '~' to Not):
    //   '(Not(seqeof))'  ([~seqeof] loop)  -> '(seqeof)'         (the double negative collapses)
    //   '(bRunning)'     ([bRunning] loop) -> '(Not(bRunning))'
    // Shared by both loop-collapse sites: _ChangeLegacyIndicators_Sub (below) and FixIndicatorsLoopRepeatCommand.
    Function _NegateLoopBackCondition String sCond Returns String
        String sInner

        Move (Trim(sCond)) to sCond
        If (sCond = "") ;
            Function_Return ""
        // Unwrap ONE outer parenthesis layer: '(expr)' -> 'expr' - when that pair holds the whole condition: '(A) or (B)'
        // is two groups (2026-11-01, _IsSingleParenGroup).
        If (_IsSingleParenGroup(Self, sCond) = True) ;
            Move (Trim(Mid(sCond, (Length(sCond) - 2), 2))) to sCond
        // Already negated as 'Not(x)' -> its negation is just 'x' (collapse Not(Not(x)) -> x) - when that Not covers the
        // whole condition: 'Not(A) and Not(B)' negates A alone, and its negation is no '(A) and Not(B)'.
        If (Lowercase(Left(sCond, 4)) = (Lowercase(CS_Not) + "(") and _IsSingleParenGroup(Self, Mid(sCond, Length(sCond), 4)) = True) Begin
            Move (Trim(Mid(sCond, (Length(sCond) - 5), 5))) to sInner   // text inside Not( ... )
            Function_Return ("(" + sInner + ")")
        End
        Function_Return ("(" + CS_Not + "(" + sCond + "))")
    End_Function

    Function _ChangeLegacyIndicators_Sub tTokenizer TokenizerData String sOverStrikeLine Boolean ByRef bChanged Returns String
        String sToken sLine sMove sIf sTo sFirstCmd sSecondCmd sFirstBoolean sSecondBoolean
        Integer iItem iSize iPos iCount iLeftParanthesis iRightParanthesis
        Boolean bHasIf bHasMove bHasTo bIndicateCmd bToPart
        tExpression Expression

        // Guard against a tokenless line (asLineTokens[0] would fault err 4509). The caller normally ensures a
        // bracket / Indicate is present (so the array is non-empty), but be safe.
        If (SizeOfArray(TokenizerData.asLineTokens) = 0) ;
            Function_Return sOverStrikeLine
        Move TokenizerData.asLineTokens[iItem] to sToken
        If (Left(sToken, 1) <> "[") Begin
            Function_Return sOverStrikeLine
        End

        // Has If-statement?
        Move (TokenizerData.bHasIfCommand = True) to bHasIf
        If (bHasIf = True) Begin
            Move (SearchArray(CS_If, TokenizerData.asLineTokens, Desktop, RefFunc(DFSTRICMP))) to iItem
            If (iItem <> -1) Begin
                Move TokenizerData.asLineTokens[iItem] to sIf
            End
        End
        Else Begin
            Move CS_If to sIf
        End

        // Has an "Indicate" command?
        Move TokenizerData.BooleanIndicator.bHasIndicateCommand to bIndicateCmd

        // Has Move-statement?
        Move (SearchArray(CS_Move, TokenizerData.asLineTokens, Desktop, RefFunc(DFSTRICMP))) to iItem
        If (iItem <> -1) Begin
            Move TokenizerData.asLineTokens[iItem] to sMove
        End
        Else Begin
            Move CS_Move to sMove
        End
        Move (iItem <> -1) to bHasMove

        // Has To-statement?
        Move (SearchArray(CS_To, TokenizerData.asLineTokens, Desktop, RefFunc(DFSTRICMP))) to iItem
        If (iItem <> -1) Begin
            Move TokenizerData.asLineTokens[iItem] to sTo
        End
        Else Begin
            Move CS_To to sTo
        End
        Move (iItem <> -1) to bHasTo

        Move TokenizerData.FirstLeftCommand.sCode  to sFirstCmd
        Move TokenizerData.SecondLeftCommand.sCode to sSecondCmd
        Move TokenizerData.BooleanIndicator.FirstBoolean.sCode  to sFirstBoolean
        Move 0 to iItem

        // Take care of the part before the "to" keyword:
        Case Begin
            Case (Lowercase(sFirstCmd) = Lowercase(CS_Indicate))
                If (TokenizerData.BooleanIndicator.FirstBoolean.bHasBracket = True) Begin
                    Move (sIf * String(TokenizerData.BooleanIndicator.FirstBoolean.sCode) * String(sMove)) to sOverStrikeLine
                End
                Else Begin
                    Move sMove to sOverStrikeLine
                End
                If (TokenizerData.BooleanIndicator.AsBoolean.sCode <> "") Begin
                   Move TokenizerData.BooleanIndicator.AsBoolean.sCode to sToken
                End
                Else Begin
                    Move TokenizerData.BooleanIndicator.FirstBoolean.sCode to sToken
                End
                // If we have an expression and it contains an "IN" operator, we need to change it to "Contains",
                // else there will be a compilation error. Also swap operands: "A IN B" => "B contains A".
                If (Left(sToken, 1) = "(" and Right(sToken, 1) = ")" and Lowercase(sToken) contains Lowercase(CS_In)) Begin
                    If (Lowercase(sToken) contains (" " + Lowercase(CS_In) + " ")) Begin
                        Move (Pos((" " + Lowercase(CS_In) + " "), Lowercase(sToken))) to iPos
                        // Extract left operand (before " IN ") and right operand (after " IN "), then swap
                        Move (Mid(sToken, (iPos - 2), 2)) to sLine    // left operand (strip leading "(")
                        Move (Mid(sToken, (Length(sToken) - iPos - Length(CS_In) - 2), (iPos + Length(CS_In) + 2))) to sToken // right operand (strip trailing ")")
                        Move ("(" + Trim(sToken) + " " + CS_Contains + " " + Trim(sLine) + ")") to sToken
                    End
                End
                Append sOverStrikeLine " " sToken
                Case Break

            Case (Lowercase(sFirstCmd) = Lowercase(CS_If))
                Move sIf to sOverStrikeLine
                If (sFirstBoolean <> "") Begin
                    Move "" to sSecondBoolean
                    If (Left(sFirstBoolean, 1) <> "(") Begin
                        Append sOverStrikeLine " (" sFirstBoolean ")"
                    End
                    If (TokenizerData.BooleanIndicator.SecondBoolean.sCode <> "") Begin
                        Append sOverStrikeLine " " TokenizerData.SecondLeftCommand.sCode
                        Append sOverStrikeLine " " TokenizerData.BooleanIndicator.SecondBoolean.sCode
                    End
                    Else Begin
                        Move (Replace("(", sFirstBoolean, "")) to sFirstBoolean
                        Move (Replace(")", sFirstBoolean, "")) to sFirstBoolean
                        If (TokenizerData.BooleanIndicator.SecondBoolean.sCode <> "") Begin
                            Move TokenizerData.BooleanIndicator.SecondBoolean.sCode to sSecondBoolean
                            Move (Replace("(", sSecondBoolean, "")) to sSecondBoolean
                            Move (Replace(")", sSecondBoolean, "")) to sSecondBoolean
                        End

                        Move (SizeOfArray(TokenizerData.asLineTokens)) to iSize
                        Decrement iSize
                        Move (SearchArray(CS_If, TokenizerData.asLineTokens, Desktop, RefFunc(DFSTRICMP))) to iItem
                        Move "" to sLine       // accumulates non-expression tokens before the first expression
                        Move False to bHasMove // tracks whether the (indicator and expression) wrapper has been emitted
                        For iCount from (iItem +1) to iSize
                            Move TokenizerData.asLineTokens[iCount] to sToken
                            Move False to bToPart
                            If (Lowercase(sToken) = lowercase(CS_To) or Lowercase(sToken) = Lowercase(CS_As)) Begin
                                Move iSize to iCount // We're out of here.
                                /* THE "TO" PART BELOW WRITES IT (2026-10-31). The word was appended here as well, so
                                   '[~X] If a eq 0 Set Field_Changed_Value Field T.F to v' came out as '... T.F to to
                                   v' (error 4393). When that part has a destination to write, the word is left to it. */
                                Move (TokenizerData.BooleanIndicator.AsBoolean.sCode <> "" or TokenizerData.BooleanIndicator.ToBoolean.sCode <> "") to bToPart
                            End
                            If (bToPart = False) Begin
                                If (SizeOfArray(TokenizerData.aExpressions) <> 0) Begin
                                    // Find expression by sExpression field only (SearchArray compares all struct fields):
                                    Move -1 to iItem
                                    Move (SizeOfArray(TokenizerData.aExpressions)) to iPos
                                    Decrement iPos
                                    For iLeftParanthesis from 0 to iPos
                                        If (TokenizerData.aExpressions[iLeftParanthesis].sExpression = sToken) Begin
                                            Move iLeftParanthesis to iItem
                                            Move iPos to iLeftParanthesis  // break
                                        End
                                    Loop
                                    If (iItem <> -1) Begin
                                        If (Lowercase(sToken) = Lowercase(CS_In)) Begin
                                            Move CS_Contains to sToken
                                        End
                                        If (sLine <> "") Begin
                                            // Non-expression tokens precede the expression — wrap all together:
                                            If (sSecondBoolean = "") Begin
                                                Append sOverStrikeLine " (" (String(sFirstBoolean)) " and (" (Trim(sLine)) " " sToken "))"
                                            End
                                            Else Begin
                                                Append sOverStrikeLine " (" (String(sFirstBoolean)) " and " (String(sSecondBoolean)) " and (" (Trim(sLine)) " " sToken "))"
                                            End
                                            Move "" to sLine
                                        End
                                        Else Begin
                                            If (sSecondBoolean = "") Begin
                                                Append sOverStrikeLine " (" (String(sFirstBoolean)) " and " sToken ")"
                                            End
                                            Else Begin
                                                Append sOverStrikeLine " (" (String(sFirstBoolean)) " and " (String(sSecondBoolean)) " and " sToken ")"
                                            End
                                        End
                                        Move True to bHasMove  // wrapper has been emitted
                                    End
                                    Else Begin
                                        If (bHasMove = False) Begin
                                            // Before first expression — accumulate for possible prefix wrapping:
                                            If (sLine = "") Begin
                                                Move sToken to sLine
                                            End
                                            Else Begin
                                                Append sLine " " sToken
                                            End
                                        End
                                        Else Begin
                                            // After expression wrapper — append remaining tokens directly:
                                            Append sOverStrikeLine " " sToken
                                        End
                                    End
                                End
                                Else Begin
                                    Append sOverStrikeLine " " sToken
                                End
                            End
                        Loop
                        // If pre-expression tokens were collected but no expression was found, append them:
                        If (sLine <> "") Begin
                            Append sOverStrikeLine " " (Trim(sLine))
                        End
                    End
                End
                Case Break

            Case (Lowercase(sFirstCmd) = Lowercase(CS_Move))
                Move TokenizerData.BooleanIndicator.FirstBoolean.sCode to sToken
                Move (sIf * String(sToken) * String(sMove)) to sOverstrikeLine
                If (TokenizerData.bHasEndSemiColon = True) Begin
                    Move TokenizerData.sLine to sLine
                    Get _RemoveEndComment sLine to sLine
                    Move (Pos(" " + Lowercase(CS_Move) + " ", Lowercase(sLine))) to iPos
                    If (iPos <> 0) Begin
                        Move (Mid(sLine, Length(sLine), (iPos + Length(CS_Move) + 2))) to sToken
                        Append sOverStrikeLine " " sToken
                    End
                End
                Else Begin
                    Append sOverStrikeLine " " TokenizerData.BooleanIndicator.SecondBoolean.sCode
                End
                Case Break

            Case (Lowercase(sFirstCmd) = Lowercase(CS_Repeat))
                If (TokenizerData.BooleanIndicator.FirstBoolean.sCode <> "") Begin
                    Move CS_While to sOverStrikeLine
                    If (Left(TokenizerData.BooleanIndicator.FirstBoolean.sCode, 1) <> "(") Begin
                        Move ("(" + TokenizerData.BooleanIndicator.FirstBoolean.sCode + ")") to TokenizerData.BooleanIndicator.FirstBoolean.sCode
                    End
                    Append sOverStrikeLine " " TokenizerData.BooleanIndicator.FirstBoolean.sCode
                End
                Else Begin
                    Move sFirstCmd to sOverStrikeLine
                End
                Case Break

            Case (Lowercase(sFirstCmd) = Lowercase(CS_While))
                Move sFirstCmd to sOverStrikeLine
                If (TokenizerData.BooleanIndicator.SecondBoolean.sCode <> "") Begin
                    Move TokenizerData.BooleanIndicator.SecondBoolean.sCode to sToken
                End
                Else Begin
                    Move TokenizerData.BooleanIndicator.FirstBoolean.sCode to sToken
                End
                Append sOverStrikeLine " " sToken
                Case Break

            Case (Lowercase(sFirstCmd) = Lowercase(CS_Until) or Lowercase(sFirstCmd) = Lowercase(CS_Loop))
                Move sFirstCmd to sOverstrikeLine
                If (Lowercase(sFirstCmd) = Lowercase(CS_Until)) Begin
                    If (TokenizerData.BooleanIndicator.SecondBoolean.sCode <> "") Begin
                        Move TokenizerData.BooleanIndicator.SecondBoolean.sCode to sToken
                    End
                    Else Begin
                        Move TokenizerData.BooleanIndicator.FirstBoolean.sCode to sToken
                    End
                    Append sOverStrikeLine " " sToken
                End
                // '[cond] Loop' is a conditional loop-BACK; its modern form is the post-test 'Until (Not(cond))',
                // NOT a bare 'Loop' (which loses the exit test -> infinite loop; LegacyApp files.nui '[~seqeof] loop'
                // -> 'Until (seqeof)' after the double-negative collapse). A bare 'Loop' with no indicator stays.
                // Two booleans, '[A B] Loop' / '[A] [B] Loop', loop back while BOTH hold (2026-11-01): the first alone
                // was the exit test, and '[Found] [~Ok] Loop' ended its loop on Found alone.
                Else If (TokenizerData.BooleanIndicator.FirstBoolean.sCode <> "") Begin
                    Get _ConstructDoubleBooleanExpression TokenizerData to sToken
                    If (sToken = "") ;
                        Move TokenizerData.BooleanIndicator.FirstBoolean.sCode to sToken
                    Get _NegateLoopBackCondition sToken to sToken
                    Move (CS_Until * sToken) to sOverstrikeLine
                End
                Case Break

            Case (TokenizerData.BooleanIndicator.FirstBoolean.sCode <> "")
                Move (SizeOfArray(TokenizerData.asLineTokens)) to iSize
                Decrement iSize
                Move CS_If to sOverstrikeLine
                If (TokenizerData.BooleanIndicator.FirstBoolean.bDoubleBoolean = True) Begin
                    Get _ConstructDoubleBooleanExpression TokenizerData to sToken
                    Append sOverStrikeLine " " sToken
                    Move 0 to iSize
                End
                Else Begin
                    Append sOverStrikeLine " " sFirstBoolean
                End
                If (sFirstCmd = "") Begin
                    Increment iItem
                    If (TokenizerData.BooleanIndicator.FirstBoolean.bHasNot = True) Begin
                        Increment iItem
                    End
                    // Guard the index: a bare "[indicator]" with no command token after it leaves iItem past the
                    // last token, so this unguarded read faulted err 4509 "Referenced Array Index Out of Bounds".
                    // Out of range -> leave sFirstCmd "" (nothing to transform after the indicator).
                    If (iItem < SizeOfArray(TokenizerData.asLineTokens)) ;
                        Move TokenizerData.asLineTokens[iItem] to sFirstCmd
                End
                Append sOverstrikeLine CS_S sFirstCmd
                // Find the command's index directly. The old 'iItem = 1 (+1 if negated)' assumed the negation
                // adds a token ([Not X] = two tokens), but the tilde form [~X] is ONE token - so for
                // '[~seqeof] increment rval#' iItem over-shot to 'rval#' and the arg loop below dropped it,
                // emitting 'If (Not(seqeof)) increment' (#$ ARGUMENT REQUIRED -> control-block cascade; LegacyApp
                // files.nui). SearchArray is token-structure-agnostic, so it is correct for [Not X] AND [~X].
                Move (SearchArray(sFirstCmd, TokenizerData.asLineTokens, Desktop, RefFunc(DFSTRICMP))) to iItem
                If (iItem = -1) ;
                    Move 1 to iItem
                If (iSize > iItem) Begin
                    Increment iItem
                    While (iItem <= iSize)
                        Move TokenizerData.asLineTokens[iItem] to sToken
                        If (Lowercase(sToken) = Lowercase(CS_To)) Begin
                            Move iSize to iItem // Get out of here
                        End
                        Else If (Trim(sToken) <> "") Begin
                            Append sOverstrikeLine CS_S sToken
                        End
                        Increment iItem
                    Loop
                End
                Case Break

            Case Else

        Case End

        // "To" part:
        If (TokenizerData.BooleanIndicator.AsBoolean.sCode <> "") Begin
            Append sOverStrikeLine " " sTo
            Move TokenizerData.BooleanIndicator.SecondBoolean.sCode to sToken
            Get ReplaceParanthesis sToken to sToken
            Append sOverStrikeLine " " sToken
        End
        Else If (TokenizerData.BooleanIndicator.ToBoolean.sCode <> "") Begin
            Append sOverStrikeLine " " sTo
            Move TokenizerData.BooleanIndicator.ToBoolean.sCode to sToken
            Get _NumberOfParanthesis sToken (&iLeftParanthesis) to iRightParanthesis
            If (iLeftParanthesis = 1 or iRightParanthesis = 1) Begin
                Get ReplaceParanthesis sToken to sToken
            End
            Append sOverStrikeLine " " sToken
        End

        Function_Return sOverStrikeLine
    End_Function

    // ====================================================================
    // Tokenizer orchestrator (MAIN PUBLIC MESSAGE of this layer)
    // ====================================================================

    // Tokenizer helper function for multiline strings. LineScan is the Tokenizer's scan of the line (ScanSourceLine)
    // from the string open at its start, so the line is not read again here.
    Function HandleMultiLineString tTokenizer TokenizerData tLineScan LineScan Returns tTokenizer
        Boolean bFound
        Integer iStartPos iEndPos iType

        // Check if currently processing a multi-line string
        Get piMultiLineStringType to iType
        If (iType <> MLS_None) Begin
            // Does the line end it? A """ string on a line that starts with """, an @-string at its FIRST closing
            // quote, wherever that stands (measured 2026-10-29 - an @-string used to end only on a line that ENDED
            // in its quote, so 'World" to sText' left it open and the code after it read as text)
            If (iType = MLS_AtQuoteOpen) ;
                Move (Right(TokenizerData.sOverstrikeLine, 1) <> '"') to bFound
            Else ;
                Move (LineScan.iCloseAt > 0) to bFound
            If (bFound) Begin
                // End of multi-line string found, reset state - unless the code after an @-string's closing
                // quote opens the next string (a """ closer opens none)
                Set piMultiLineStringType to MLS_None
                Move False to TokenizerData.bIsInDF23MultiLineString
                If (_AtStringQuote(Self, iType) <> "" and LineScan.sOpenOut <> "") Begin
                    Set piMultiLineStringType to (_StringTypeOf(Self, LineScan.sOpenOut, TokenizerData.sOverstrikeLine))
                    Move True to TokenizerData.bIsInDF23MultiLineString
                End
                Move True to TokenizerData.bLineIsReady
                Function_Return TokenizerData
            End
            // Multi-line string continues - this line is string content, not code
            Else Begin
                Move True to TokenizerData.bIsInDF23MultiLineString
                Move True to TokenizerData.bLineIsReady
                Set pbKeepLineAsWritten to True
                Function_Return TokenizerData
            End
        End
        Else Begin
            /* Does this line open one? The line scanner says (ScanSourceLine, measured on DataFlex 26): a line
               that ENDS in a """ outside every string, or one that leaves an @"... / @SQL"... / @'... / @SQL'...
               string open at its end - after any statement, not only a Move. Until 2026-10-29 an @" string opened
               only after a Move or through a second test further down (both gone), and an @' string not at all. */
            If (LineScan.sOpenOut <> "") Begin
                Set piMultiLineStringType to (_StringTypeOf(Self, LineScan.sOpenOut, TokenizerData.sOverstrikeLine))
                Set pbLastLineOpenedString to True
                Move True to TokenizerData.bIsInDF23MultiLineString
                Move False to TokenizerData.bLineIsReady
                Function_Return TokenizerData
            End
        End

        // Check for SQL strings starting with @SQL
        If (Pos('@SQL', TokenizerData.sOverstrikeLine) > 0) Begin
            // Find the position of the start and end of the triple-quoted string
            Move (Pos('@SQL"""', TokenizerData.sOverstrikeLine)) to iStartPos
            Move (RightPos('"""', TokenizerData.sOverstrikeLine)) to iEndPos

            // Check if both start and end are on the same line and properly positioned. (An open one is the
            // opener rule's above, and so is every open @-string.)
            If (iStartPos > 0 and iEndPos > iStartPos + 6) Begin
                // Single-line SQL triple-quoted string
                Set piMultiLineStringType to MLS_None
                Move False to TokenizerData.bIsInDF23MultiLineString
                Move True to TokenizerData.bLineIsReady
                Function_Return TokenizerData
            End
        End

        // Default return for lines not identified as multi-line strings
        Set piMultiLineStringType to MLS_None
        Function_Return TokenizerData
    End_Function

    // * Dummy function for the Studio's Code Explorer *
    // *** MAIN PUBLIC MESSAGE for this system class is the Tokenizer ***
    Procedure MAIN_PUBLIC_MESSAGE_TOKENIZER
    End_Procedure

    /* Syntax:
       Get Tokenizer sSourceLine to TokenizerData (struct variable)
    It splits up the passed source line (sLine) to members of the tTokenizer struct.
    It then sets the pTokenizer struct property, so that any message of the
    cRefactorFuncLib class can use those member values to do their thing.

    Note: If the line is a compound statement (one that spans over several lines),
          e.g. it contains a ";" or one '"""', the function will set the
          property piMultiLineStringType.
    */
    Function _TokenizeLine String sLine Returns tTokenizer
        tTokenizer TokenizerData
        tExpression[] aExpression
        Boolean bFound bEnd bInMultiLineString bIsDoubleQuoteStart bIsOpenCommand bStatus bCloser bReread bFresh
        Integer iType
        String sQuote
        tLineScan LineScan Fresh

        Move sLine to TokenizerData.sLine
        Set pbKeepLineAsWritten to False
        /* INSIDE A DF 23 """ STRING THE BODY IS TEXT, whatever it holds (2026-10-24). Decided before every other
           test: a '#HEADER', a '/*' (a CSS or SQL comment), a '/api' or a '// x' in the string must not open a
           header region, a block comment or a report image - a '/*' line used to clear the string state, so the
           rest of the body read as code. The raw line decides (measured on DataFlex 26: a closing """ starts its
           line, and text before a """ is error 4346, so no body line ends in one); the scope flags come from the
           properties, as on the other finished lines. Two lines take the normal path instead. The CLOSING line:
           its code after the """ fills the fields a whole-method reader needs (RemoveUnusedLocals finds a local
           used there in sOverstrikeLine, and a ';' on it continues the next line), and HandleMultiLineString
           ends the string. And the OPENING line once more - a fix changed it and the engine re-tokenizes it - so
           it is tokenized as the first time, not read as body. A body line is marked pbKeepLineAsWritten.
           AN @-STRING'S TEXT the same way (2026-10-29): a line without its closing quote is text whole - nothing
           escapes that quote (measured on DataFlex 26), so a '// x', a '#HEADER' or a '/*' there is text too - and
           its opening line read again opens it again (pbLastLineOpenedString). Its CLOSING line holds text too,
           before the quote, so it is marked pbKeepLineAsWritten as well - its code after the quote is the line
           functions' no more than a """ closer's is (the line is ready): NormalizeArrayNotation, reading it as code
           from its first character, rewrote 'String [] asX" to s' (measured 2026-10-29). A closing line of either
           kind (bCloser) skips the comment, header, image and block-comment tests below: its text is none of those,
           and a """ closer followed by + "/*" no longer opens a block comment. The line is read by the line scanner
           (ScanSourceLine), once from the string open at its start (LineScan) and once from its
           first character (Fresh: its block comment, its end comment, the string it opens), each only when asked. */
        Get pbLastLineOpenedString to bReread
        Set pbLastLineOpenedString to False
        Get piMultiLineStringType to iType
        Get _AtStringQuote iType to sQuote
        Move False to bCloser
        Move False to bFresh
        If (iType = MLS_TripleQuote or iType = MLS_SQLTripleQuote) Begin
            // The opening line read again: an opener ends in """, so only such a line is read for it
            If (Right(Trim(Replaces((Character(9)), sLine, " ")), 3) = '"""') Begin
                Get ScanSourceLine sLine "" False to Fresh
                Move True to bFresh
            End
            If (bFresh = True and Fresh.sOpenOut = '"""') Begin
                Set piMultiLineStringType to MLS_None
            End
            Else Begin
                Get ScanSourceLine sLine '"""' False to LineScan
                If (LineScan.iCloseAt = 0) Begin
                    Get _CollectTokenizerFromProperties TokenizerData to TokenizerData
                    Move True to TokenizerData.bLineIsReady
                    Set pbKeepLineAsWritten to True
                    Set pTokenizer to TokenizerData
                    Function_Return TokenizerData
                End
                Move True to bCloser
            End
        End
        Else If (sQuote <> "") Begin
            If (bReread = True) Begin
                Get ScanSourceLine sLine "" False to Fresh
                Move True to bFresh
            End
            If (bFresh = True and Fresh.sOpenOut <> "") Begin
                Set piMultiLineStringType to MLS_None
                Move "" to sQuote
            End
            Else Begin
                Get ScanSourceLine sLine sQuote False to LineScan
                If (LineScan.iCloseAt = 0) Begin
                    Get _CollectTokenizerFromProperties TokenizerData to TokenizerData
                    Move True to TokenizerData.bLineIsReady
                    Set pbKeepLineAsWritten to True
                    Set pTokenizer to TokenizerData
                    Function_Return TokenizerData
                End
                Move True to bCloser
                Set pbKeepLineAsWritten to True
            End
        End
        // Place all cases for when we are done at the top of
        // of this function so we can jump out.
        //
        // A #HEADER ... #ENDHEADER region is PRECOMPILED into <program>.pkd and is not ours
        // to refactor - see _IsHeaderDeclaration in cRefactorUtilities.pkg for what rewriting
        // one costs (389 phantom compile errors). bLineIsReady is the universal "hands off
        // this line" signal every refactoring function already tests first, so this ONE gate
        // protects the whole region - including the #COMMAND macro bodies that live in it.
        // Deliberately the first test in this group: it must not be possible for the comment/
        // blank/open-command gate below to consume the #ENDHEADER line and leave the flag ON.
        // Every line of the region, the #HEADER and #ENDHEADER lines too, is marked pbKeepLineAsWritten (2026-10-29):
        // a function that tests no bLineIsReady still never gets one.
        If (pbInHeader(Self) = True) Begin
            Get _IsHeaderEnd TokenizerData.sLine to bFound
            If (bFound = True) Begin
                Set pbInHeader to False
            End
            Move True to TokenizerData.bLineIsReady
            Set pbKeepLineAsWritten to True
            Set pTokenizer to TokenizerData
            Function_Return TokenizerData
        End
        Else If (bCloser = False) Begin
            Get _IsHeaderDeclaration TokenizerData.sLine to bFound
            If (bFound = True) Begin
                Set pbInHeader to True
                Move True to TokenizerData.bLineIsReady
                Set pbKeepLineAsWritten to True
                Set pTokenizer to TokenizerData
                Function_Return TokenizerData
            End
        End

        /* A BLOCK COMMENT'S AND A REPORT IMAGE'S TEXT ARE KEPT AS WRITTEN TOO (2026-10-30), as the whole-file
           functions' guard keeps them (cRefactorFuncLib's _CommentAndImageTextFlagsOf): a line wholly inside a
           block comment (no closing marker on it) and an image's text - not a page's name line, which
           RemoveResidentImageOption edits, nor the image's closing marker. The tokenizer already reads both as
           ready (bLineIsReady), but a function that reads the raw line tests nothing: on a workspace copy
           AddUseFileExtension made 'Use the file' in a comment 'Use the.pkg file', and another line function made
           'e.g. [Select]' there 'e.g.[Select]'. Marked here, from the state the line before left, so a blank or a
           '//' line inside one is marked as well. */
        If (bCloser = False) Begin
            If (pbIsInDF23MultiLineComment(Self) = True and Pos("*/", sLine) = 0) ;
                Set pbKeepLineAsWritten to True
            If (pbIsInPage(Self) = True and IsImageStart(Self, sLine) = False and IsImageEnd(Self, sLine) = False) ;
                Set pbKeepLineAsWritten to True
        End

        // Standard commented lines that uses double-slashes "//" - not inside a block comment, where the test
        // further down reads every line: a '// ... */' line ends the comment (2026-10-30 - this returned first, so
        // the comment stayed open in the tokenizer's state and the code below such a line read as comment).
        If (bCloser = False and pbIsInDF23MultiLineComment(Self) = False) Begin
            Get _IsCommentLine TokenizerData.sLine to TokenizerData.bIsComment
            Get _IsBlankLine   TokenizerData.sLine to TokenizerData.bIsBlank
            Get _IsOpenCommand TokenizerData.sLine to bIsOpenCommand
        End
        If (TokenizerData.bIsComment = True or TokenizerData.bIsBlank = True or bIsOpenCommand = True) Begin
            Get _CollectTokenizerFromProperties TokenizerData to TokenizerData
            Move True to TokenizerData.bLineIsReady
            Set pTokenizer to TokenizerData
            Function_Return TokenizerData
        End

        // Note. This needs to before the new DF23 multi-line string/comment logic.
        // Old DataFlex 2.3 and earlier syntax that used "image pages". Starts with "/MyPage" and ends with a slash-star marker.
        // We will do nothing with such lines.
        If (pbIsInPage(Self) = True) Begin
            Get IsImageEnd TokenizerData.sLine to bFound
            If (bFound = True) Begin
                Send _ClearRefactoringProperties
                Move True to TokenizerData.bLineIsReady
                Set pTokenizer to TokenizerData
                Function_Return TokenizerData
            End
            Else Begin
                Move True to TokenizerData.bIsInImage
                Move True to TokenizerData.bLineIsReady
                Set pTokenizer to TokenizerData
                Function_Return TokenizerData
            End
        End
        // Not inside a block comment: a commented-out '/Body' line is comment text, as the file walk reads it
        // (ScanSourceFile tests the comment first; 2026-10-30)
        Else If (pbIsInPage(Self) = False and bCloser = False and pbIsInDF23MultiLineComment(Self) = False) Begin
            Get IsImageStart TokenizerData.sLine to TokenizerData.bIsInImage
            If (TokenizerData.bIsInImage = True) Begin
                Send _ClearRefactoringProperties
                Set pbIsInPage to True
                Move True to TokenizerData.bIsInImage
                Move True to TokenizerData.bLineIsReady
                Set pTokenizer to TokenizerData
                Function_Return TokenizerData
            End
        End

        // DF 2023 block-style multi-line comment (slash-star opens, star-slash closes).
        If (pbIsInDF23MultiLineComment(Self) = True) Begin
            Get _IsDF23CommentEnd TokenizerData.sLine to bFound
            /* ONLY THE COMMENT ENDS HERE (2026-10-30), as only the object ends at an End_Object (below). This
               called _ClearRefactoringProperties, which wipes every scope flag, so a block comment inside a method
               ended the method for the tokenizer and the scope-aware functions went blind for the rest of it:
               UnicodeStringToPointer left the Move after such a comment as it was. A comment line - its closing
               line too - carries the scope it stands in. */
            If (bFound = True) ;
                Set pbIsInDF23MultiLineComment to False
            Get _CollectTokenizerFromProperties TokenizerData to TokenizerData
            Move True to TokenizerData.bIsInDF23MultiLineComment
            Get _DF23CommentOverwrite TokenizerData.sLine to TokenizerData.sOverstrikeLine
            Move True to TokenizerData.bIsComment
            Move True to TokenizerData.bLineIsReady
            Set pTokenizer to TokenizerData
            Function_Return TokenizerData
        End
        Else If (bCloser = False) Begin
            If (bFresh = False) Begin
                Get ScanSourceLine sLine "" False to Fresh
                Move True to bFresh
            End
            Move (Fresh.iBlockStartAt > 0) to TokenizerData.bIsInDF23MultiLineComment
            If (TokenizerData.bIsInDF23MultiLineComment = True) Begin
                Get _DF23CommentOverwrite TokenizerData.sLine to TokenizerData.sOverstrikeLine
                // The scope the comment stands in is kept: its opening line is no end of a method either (above)
                Get _CollectTokenizerFromProperties TokenizerData to TokenizerData
                Move True to TokenizerData.bIsInDF23MultiLineComment
                // A SINGLE-LINE "/* ... */" opens AND closes right here - the ubiquitous VDF IDE
                // marker ("/* Do NOT REMOVE THIS LINE: IDE GENERATED CODE WILL GO HERE */" -
                // WinServ's GBE.dg, Nils 2026-07-17). Without this same-line close check the
                // sticky flag stayed ON to end-of-file and EVERY converter below the marker
                // silently skipped (the scan flagged the rows, the run changed 0 lines). The
                // line itself reads as a comment either way; only the CARRY-OVER is gated. The comment ends at its
                // first "*/", quotes or not: "/* every row's element */" carried over too (2026-10-30).
                If (Fresh.bBlockOpenOut = True) ;
                    Set pbIsInDF23MultiLineComment to True
                Move True to TokenizerData.bIsComment
                Move True to TokenizerData.bLineIsReady
                Set pTokenizer to TokenizerData
                Function_Return TokenizerData
            End
        End

        // Get the indentation part
        Get _Indentation (&TokenizerData) to TokenizerData.sIndentation
        // The end comment, from the line's scan: on an @-string's closing line only the code after the string can
        // hold one; any other line - a """ closer too, as before - is read from its first character
        If (bCloser = True and sQuote <> "") Begin
            Move (_ScannedEndComment(Self, sLine, LineScan)) to TokenizerData.sEndComment
        End
        Else Begin
            If (bFresh = False) Begin
                Get ScanSourceLine sLine "" False to Fresh
                Move True to bFresh
            End
            Move (_ScannedEndComment(Self, sLine, Fresh)) to TokenizerData.sEndComment
            If (bCloser = False) ;
                Move Fresh to LineScan
        End

        // This will overstrike string constant characters with "_" characters for a "some text" and
        // '+' characters for a 'some other text'
        // This is so the refactoring functions does not get confused by the content of string literals.
        // E.g. Move "We will *move* some of the warehouse" to sText is changed to: Move "________________________________" to sText
        // Thus, most refactoring funtions should be using the sOverstrikeLine member value, rather then the
        // original sLine content itself.
        Get _OverstrikeStrings (&TokenizerData) to TokenizerData.sOverstrikeLine

        Get _IsPrnLine TokenizerData.sOverstrikeLine to bFound
        If (bFound = True) Begin
            Move True to TokenizerData.bLineIsReady
            Set pTokenizer to TokenizerData
            Function_Return TokenizerData
        End

        Get _IsGotoLabel TokenizerData.sOverstrikeLine to bFound
        If (bFound = True) Begin
            Move True to TokenizerData.bLineIsReady
            Set pTokenizer to TokenizerData
            Function_Return TokenizerData
        End

        // Old school multi-line, ending with a semi-colon (;). FIRST the carried answer - does THIS
        // line continue the previous one? - read before the property is overwritten with this line's
        // own ending. _CollectTokenizerFromProperties fills the same field, but only on the non-code
        // branches above; an ordinary code line reaches it here (2026-09-17, the split Indicate).
        Get pbIsInSemiColonMultiLineString to TokenizerData.bIsContinuationLine
        Get _HasLineEndSemiColon TokenizerData.sOverstrikeLine to TokenizerData.bHasEndSemiColon
        Set pbIsInSemiColonMultiLineString to TokenizerData.bHasEndSemiColon

        // DF 23 Multi-line strings are lines that starts with a @, @SQL or """
        // The property piMultiLineStringType is set to <> MLS_None as soon as such a
        // multi-line string is started (and not ended):
        Get HandleMultiLineString TokenizerData LineScan to TokenizerData
        If (TokenizerData.bLineIsReady = True) Begin
            // Stored like every other finished line (2026-10-24): without it a multi-line string's body and
            // closing lines left pTokenizer holding the line before, which said "code" - and every line
            // function reads pTokenizer, so they acted on the string's text.
            Set pTokenizer to TokenizerData
            Function_Return TokenizerData
        End

        // *** End of tests that sets the TokenizerData.bLineIsReady = True.

        // Note: This also fills the TokenizerData.aExpressions member with data.
        Get _SplitSourceLineToTokens (&TokenizerData) to TokenizerData

        // Set properties to indicate if we are inside a function or a procedure.
        // Needs to be after calls to _OverstrikeStrings & _SplitSourceLineToTokens
        If (pbInFunction(Self) = True) Begin
            // A method closes on EITHER End_Function or End_Procedure. The DataFlex
            // compiler tolerates a Function closed with End_Procedure (and vice
            // versa); if we required the exact keyword, the in-function flag would
            // get STUCK on the mismatch and every later line in the file would be
            // misclassified. (That is what hid cJSONParser._ParseValue's End_Procedure
            // from cUnicodeStringToPointer.) A truly MISSING end keyword is not
            // handled here yet - the existing "new declaration mid-method" branch is
            // left as-is pending a separately tested change.
            If (Lowercase(TokenizerData.asLineTokens[0]) = (Lowercase(CS_FunctionEnd)) or Lowercase(TokenizerData.asLineTokens[0]) = (Lowercase(CS_ProcedureEnd))) Begin
                Move False to TokenizerData.bIsInFunction
                Set pbInFunction to False
                Send _ClearMethodScopeProperties
                Move True to TokenizerData.bLineIsReady
                Set pTokenizer to TokenizerData
                Function_Return TokenizerData
            End
            Else Begin
                Move True to TokenizerData.bIsInFunction
                Get _IsProcedureDeclaration TokenizerData.sOverstrikeLine to bStatus
                If (bStatus = True) Begin
                    Move True to TokenizerData.bLineIsReady
                    Set pTokenizer to TokenizerData
                    Function_Return TokenizerData
                End
            End
        End
        Else Begin
            Get _IsFunctionDeclaration TokenizerData.sOverstrikeLine to TokenizerData.bIsInFunction
            Set pbInFunction to TokenizerData.bIsInFunction
            If (TokenizerData.bIsInFunction = True) Begin
                Move True to TokenizerData.bLineIsReady
                Set pTokenizer to TokenizerData
                Function_Return TokenizerData
            End
        End

        If (pbInProcedure(Self) = True) Begin
            // A method closes on EITHER End_Procedure or End_Function (the DataFlex
            // compiler tolerates the mismatch); requiring the exact keyword would
            // leave the in-procedure flag stuck on a Procedure closed with
            // End_Function. (Symmetric with the function branch above.)
            If (Lowercase(TokenizerData.asLineTokens[0]) = (Lowercase(CS_ProcedureEnd)) or Lowercase(TokenizerData.asLineTokens[0]) = (Lowercase(CS_FunctionEnd))) Begin
                Move False to TokenizerData.bIsInProcedure
                Set pbInProcedure to False
                Send _ClearMethodScopeProperties
                Move True to TokenizerData.bLineIsReady
                Set pTokenizer to TokenizerData
                Function_Return TokenizerData
            End
            Else Begin
                Move True to TokenizerData.bIsInProcedure
                Get _IsProcedureDeclaration TokenizerData.sOverstrikeLine to bStatus
                If (bStatus = True) Begin
                    Move True to TokenizerData.bLineIsReady
                    Set pTokenizer to TokenizerData
                    Function_Return TokenizerData
                End
            End
        End
        Else Begin
            Get _IsProcedureDeclaration TokenizerData.sOverstrikeLine to TokenizerData.bIsInProcedure
            Set pbInProcedure to TokenizerData.bIsInProcedure
            If (TokenizerData.bIsInProcedure = True) Begin
                Move True to TokenizerData.bLineIsReady
                Set pTokenizer to TokenizerData
                Function_Return TokenizerData
            End
        End

        If (pbInCommand(Self) = True) Begin
            Get _IsCommandEnd TokenizerData.sLine to bFound
            If (bFound = True) Begin
                Send _ClearRefactoringProperties
                Move True to TokenizerData.bLineIsReady
                Set pTokenizer to TokenizerData
                Function_Return TokenizerData
            End
            Else Begin
                Move True to TokenizerData.bIsInCommand
            End
        End
        Else Begin
            Get _IsCommandDeclaration TokenizerData.sOverstrikeLine to TokenizerData.bIsInCommand
            Set pbInCommand to TokenizerData.bIsInCommand
        End

        If (pbInClass(Self) = True) Begin
            Get _IsClassEnd TokenizerData.sLine to bFound
            If (bFound = True) Begin
                Send _ClearRefactoringProperties
                Move True  to TokenizerData.bLineIsReady
                Set pTokenizer to TokenizerData
                Function_Return TokenizerData
            End
            Else Begin
                Move True to TokenizerData.bIsInClass
            End
        End
        Else Begin
            Get _IsClassDeclaration TokenizerData.sOverstrikeLine to TokenizerData.bIsInClass
            Set pbInClass to TokenizerData.bIsInClass
        End

        If (pbInStruct(Self) = True) Begin
            Get _IsStructEnd TokenizerData.sLine to bFound
            If (bFound = True) Begin
                Send _ClearRefactoringProperties
                Move True  to TokenizerData.bLineIsReady
                Set pTokenizer to TokenizerData
                Function_Return TokenizerData
            End
            Else Begin
                Move True to TokenizerData.bIsInStruct
            End
        End
        Else Begin
            Get _IsStructDeclaration TokenizerData.sOverstrikeLine to TokenizerData.bIsInStruct
            Set pbInStruct to TokenizerData.bIsInStruct
        End

        If (pbInObject(Self) = True) Begin
            Get _IsObjectEnd TokenizerData.sOverstrikeLine to bFound
            If (bFound = True) Begin
                // An Object is legally declared INSIDE a Procedure/Function body
                // (a common legacy pattern: "Object oHasher is a cCryptographer"
                // + End_Object mid-method). This used to call
                // _ClearRefactoringProperties, which wipes EVERY scope flag -
                // including the enclosing method's pbInProcedure/pbInFunction -
                // so every line AFTER the End_Object was classified as
                // outside-method and scope-aware functions (UnicodePointerToString,
                // UnicodeStringToPointer, unused-locals) went blind for the rest
                // of the method (found via a "Move <Address var> to <String var>"
                // after an embedded hasher object, 2026-07-05). Only the OBJECT
                // scope ends here; in compilable code a method inside an object
                // is always closed by its own End_ keyword first, so the blanket
                // clear was never needed for that direction.
                Set pbInObject to False
                Move True  to TokenizerData.bLineIsReady
                Set pTokenizer to TokenizerData
                Function_Return TokenizerData
            End
            Else Begin
                Move True to TokenizerData.bIsInObject
            End
        End
        Else Begin
            Get _IsObjectDeclaration TokenizerData.sOverstrikeLine to TokenizerData.bIsInObject
            Set pbInObject to TokenizerData.bIsInObject
        End

        Get IsVariableDeclarationLine TokenizerData.sOverstrikeLine to TokenizerData.bIsVariableDeclaration
        If (TokenizerData.bIsVariableDeclaration = True and (TokenizerData.bIsInFunction = True or TokenizerData.bIsInProcedure = True or TokenizerData.bIsInCommand = True)) Begin
            Set piMultiLineStringType to MLS_None
            Move False to TokenizerData.bLineIsReady
            Move False to TokenizerData.bIsInDF23MultiLineString
            Set pTokenizer to TokenizerData
            Function_Return TokenizerData
        End

        Get _HasIfCommand TokenizerData.sOverstrikeLine to TokenizerData.bHasIfCommand
        // Get start and end indicators
        // "Indicate [Select] as [not Found]" -> bHasIndicateCommand = True
        Get _ExtractLegacyBooleanContent (&TokenizerData) to TokenizerData.BooleanIndicator

        // Get the "*Move iA* to xxx" part
        Get _LeftStatement (&TokenizerData) to TokenizerData.LeftStatement
        // Get the "of xxx" part
        Get _OfStatement (&TokenizerData) to TokenizerData.OfStatement
        // Get the "to xxx" part
        Get _ToStatement (&TokenizerData) to TokenizerData.ToStatement

        Get _LeftCommand (&TokenizerData) eFirstCommand  to TokenizerData.FirstLeftCommand
        Get _LeftCommand (&TokenizerData) eSecondCommand to TokenizerData.SecondLeftCommand

        Get _FetchExpression TokenizerData.aExpressions eOfExpression    to TokenizerData.sOfExpression
        Get _FetchExpression TokenizerData.aExpressions eToExpression    to TokenizerData.sToExpression
        Get _FetchExpression TokenizerData.aExpressions eAsExpression    to TokenizerData.sAsExpression
        Get _FetchExpression TokenizerData.aExpressions eLeftExpression1 to TokenizerData.sLeftExpression1
        Get _FetchExpression TokenizerData.aExpressions eLeftExpression2 to TokenizerData.sLeftExpression2

        Get _IsPropertyDeclaration TokenizerData.sOverstrikeLine to TokenizerData.bIsPropertyDeclaration

        // Convenience: first token and count
        Move (SizeOfArray(TokenizerData.asLineTokens)) to TokenizerData.iTokenCount
        If (TokenizerData.iTokenCount > 0) Begin
            Move TokenizerData.asLineTokens[0] to TokenizerData.sFirstToken
        End

        // Statement-type flags derived from the first token
        Move (Lowercase(TokenizerData.sFirstToken) = Lowercase(CS_Move))  to TokenizerData.bIsMoveStatement
        Move (Lowercase(TokenizerData.sFirstToken) = Lowercase(CS_Get))   to TokenizerData.bIsGetStatement
        Move (Lowercase(TokenizerData.sFirstToken) = Lowercase(CS_Set))   to TokenizerData.bIsSetStatement
        Move (Lowercase(TokenizerData.sFirstToken) = Lowercase(CS_Send))  to TokenizerData.bIsSendStatement
        Move (Lowercase(TokenizerData.sFirstToken) = Lowercase(CS_Begin)) to TokenizerData.bIsBeginStatement
        Move (Lowercase(TokenizerData.sFirstToken) = "end")               to TokenizerData.bIsEndStatement
        Get _HasCommand TokenizerData.sOverstrikeLine (CS_S + CS_Else)    to TokenizerData.bHasElseStatement

        Get _LogicalOperators (&TokenizerData) to TokenizerData.OperatorsInfo

        // *** Note ***
        // Intead of calling this Tokenizer function from the cRefactorFuncLib,
        // each function should do a "Get pTokenizer to TokenizerData" and use that ready-made tokenized data,
        // that was created once for each source line by this function.
        // This tokenizer call will be made automatically by the logic in DFRefactor.src & TestBenchRefactorFunctions.src.
        Set pTokenizer to TokenizerData

        Function_Return TokenizerData
    End_Function

    /* The tokenizer (_TokenizeLine). psExecutionContext says "Tokenizer" while it runs - for the error log - and is put
       back after it (2026-11-01): run notes are filed under that property's value, the running function's name, and a
       whole-file function that tokenized a line filed every later note under "Tokenizer", which no summary prints - a
       grid converter's "objects of <subclass> left as they are" never reached a run's notes. */
    Function Tokenizer String sLine Returns tTokenizer
        tTokenizer TokenizerData
        String sContext

        Get psExecutionContext to sContext
        Set psExecutionContext to "Tokenizer"
        Get _TokenizeLine sLine to TokenizerData
        Set psExecutionContext to sContext
        Function_Return TokenizerData
    End_Function

    Function _ExtractFirstStringConstant String sLine Returns String
        String sStringConstant sChar
        Integer iPos iLength iCount
        Boolean bDoubleQuote bStop

        Move "" to sStringConstant
        Move True to bDoubleQuote
        Move False to bStop
        Move (Trim(sLine)) to sLine
        Move (Pos('"', sLine)) to iPos
        If (iPos = 0) Begin
            Move (Pos("'", sLine)) to iPos
            Move False to bDoubleQuote
        End

        If (iPos > 0) Begin
            Move (Length(sLine)) to iLength
            Increment iPos
            For iCount from iPos to iLength
                Move (Mid(sLine, 1, iCount)) to sChar
                If (sChar <> '"' and sChar <> "'" and bStop = False) Begin
                    Append sStringConstant sChar
                End
                Else Begin
                    Move (sChar = '"' or sChar = "'") to bStop
                    If (bStop = True) Begin
                        Move iLength to iCount // We're out of here.
                    End
                End
            Loop
        End
        If (bDoubleQuote = True) Begin
            Move ('"' + String(sStringConstant) + '"') to sStringConstant
        End
        Else Begin
            Move ("'" + String(sStringConstant) + "'") to sStringConstant
        End
        Function_Return sStringConstant
    End_Function

End_Class
